        "evidenceText": "Homepage | Computation + Journalism 2026 Symposium Evanston, October 2nd-3rd 2026 Computation + Journalism Symposium Homepage News Beyond the Newsroom The 2026 Computation + Journalism Symposium (C+J) is a space for anyone working at or curious about the intersection between journalists, news, and technology. The conference features a unique mix of practicing journalists, including freelancers, data journalists, and engineers in newsrooms or working on news-related products; and academics working in fields like computational social science, human-computer interaction, digital humanities, and more. In 2026 the Symposium was hosted by Northwestern University and took place in Evanston, IL on October 2-3. Opening Keynote Arvind Narayanan, Princeton University AI and journalism: skating where the puck is going Closing Keynote Casey Fiesler in Conversation with Gina Chua about AI hype and science communication See the entire symposium schedule Sponsors The Computation + Journalism Symposium 2026 gratefully acknowledges the support of our sponsors:",
