        "pageDescription": "Tiziana Alocci is an award-winning Italian-born, London-based data and new media artist whose work explores absent data and invisible phenomena by investigating what has not yet been measured. Working with data as a narrative material to explore memory and the invisible structures shaping human experience.",
        "evidenceText": "Data Artist London &mdash; Tiziana Alocci 0 MAKING THE INVISIBLE VISIBLE Tiziana works with data that don’t exist. Her practice begins with research into systems and phenomena that resist direct observation. She investigate what is missing from datasets and what remains hidden within global infrastructures. Her research develops through data, fieldwork, writing, and sound. Slide 1 Slide 1 (current slide) Slide 2 Slide 2 (current slide) Slide 3 Slide 3 (current slide) Slide 4 Slide 4 (current slide) Slide 5 Slide 5 (current slide) Environmental & Urban Change , Invisible Systems Tiziana Alocci 13/09/2026 Environmental & Urban Change , Invisible Systems Tiziana Alocci 13/09/2026 DATASONICA, 2025 A sonification engine, turning a building into an orchestra. Can architecture and environments be understood as living systems through sound? Read More Invisible Systems Tiziana Alocci 12/09/2026 Invisible Systems Tiziana Alocci 12/09/2026 Twelve miles from the coast, 2026—ongoing Read More Archival Reconstruction , Environmental & Urban Change Tiziana Alocci 25/06/2026 Archival Reconstruction , Environmental & Urban Change Tiziana Alocci 25/06/2026 EVERYTHING NOT SAVED WILL BE LOST, 2023-ongoing An ongoing research into the gradual disappearance of the sky caused by new constructions, as a framework to explore memory, culture, and urban changes. What becomes perceptible when absence, rather than presence, is measured? Read More Collective Voice , Memory & Archive Tiziana Alocci 29/03/2026 Collective Voice , Memory & Archive Tiziana Alocci 29/03/2026 Frequencies of Belonging, 2025 A collection of voice notes about the meaning of home. How can a perpetual archive of voices reshape our understanding of home as a shared and evolving construct? Read More Self as Data , Memory & Archive Tiziana Alocci 16/11/2025 Self as Data , Memory & Archive Tiziana Alocci 16/11/2025 Necessity, 2022 Transforming intimate sounds into visual systems, exploring how personal experience can be measured, structured, and reinterpreted. What remains of a lived moment when it is translated into data? Read More Self as Data , Translation of the Intangible Tiziana Alocci 23/04/2025 Self as Data , Translation of the Intangible Tiziana Alocci 23/04/2025 Emotional Geography, 2024 Sonic journaling the acoustic identity of cities. How can subjective emotional experiences be mapped and shared as collective spatial narratives? Read More Invisible Systems , Environmental & Urban Change Tiziana Alocci 23/04/2025 Invisible Systems , Environmental & Urban Change Tiziana Alocci 23/04/2025 Tokyo Love Story, 2024 A sensory journey through the electromagnetic sounds of the lights of Tokyo. What forms of urban life emerge when electromagnetic signals are treated as a sensory and emotional layer of the city? Read More Structures of Inequality Tiziana Alocci 21/04/2025 Structures of Inequality Tiziana Alocci 21/04/2025 The Shapes and Sounds of Visa Inequality, 2024-25 Translating systems of global mobility into sound and form, where data reveals the structures shaping who can move—and who cannot. What becomes perceptible when systems of inequality are translated into sound, allowing data to be felt? Read More Translation of the Intangible Tiziana Alocci 20/04/2025 Translation of the Intangible Tiziana Alocci 20/04/2025 Scented connections, 2023 Translating the invisible structures of scent into data-driven compositions, where fragrances become systems of relationships. What forms of knowledge emerge when scent—an inherently intangible experience—is translated into data and visual systems? Read More Translation of the Intangible , Environmental & Urban Change Tiziana Alocci 10/02/2025 Translation of the Intangible , Environmental & Urban Change Tiziana Alocci 10/02/2025 Nature in C Major, 2025 From material to sound: shaping an audiovisual composition from the rhythms and textures of bamboo data. How can bamboo be interpreted as a living archive, a symbol of resilience, craftsmanship and organic evolution? Read More Environmental & Urban Change , Memory & Archive , Self as Data Tiziana Alocci 09/02/2025 Environmental & Urban Change , Memory & Archive , Self as Data Tiziana Alocci 09/02/2025 Sonic Tides, 2024 When noise pollution becomes visible. In what ways can environmental noise be translated into perceptible forms that alter how we experience urban space? Read More Perception & Subjectivity Tiziana Alocci 28/09/2024 Perception & Subjectivity Tiziana Alocci 28/09/2024 Data-driven album cover, 2019-23 From listening to form: translating the anatomy of sound into data-driven visual compositions. When sound is made visible, what is preserved—and what is reinterpreted through perception? Read More",
