        "evidenceText": "The map your business runs on: AI-native GIS | Felt Skip to content AM JS RK +3 Pothole reports Open 4 Filled this week 3 AM Amina 12 min ago Four open on County Rd 9. Can we fill them before Friday? JS J. Soto Just now Patch truck’s on the way, starting from the north end. Reply… JS Which warehouses within 200 m of the rail yard have leases ending this year? Leases ending 2026 Warehouses 3 Within 200 m of rail Floor area 412,000 sq ft Pole P-4471 Material Wood · class 3 Installed 1998 Inspected Just now Photos 3 Solar siting 100-year floodplain Woodland Setbacks Arrays 428 ac Fits on the site 86 MW Field 12 · North pivot Crop Soybeans Area 142 ac Soil moisture 18% Irrigation Running Legend List Water network Water mains 84.2 mi Hydrants 612 Critical facilities 9 Water main WM-2231 Material Cast iron Installed 1962 Condition 3 / 5 Replace 2027 Candidate sites Candidates 3 Competitors 6 5-min drive Site A · Pad, 1.4 ac People in 5 min 36,400 Median income $76k Competitors 3 in zone Score 91 AI-native GIS The spatial infrastructure your business runs on From the field to the office, your team communicates on the same map in real time . Ask Felt AI a question in plain language and get the answer as a map. Every asset your crews touch, logged on the map with the photos to prove it. Layer and analyze data to find the best location for your project. The full picture of any site, from aerial imagery to live readings, wherever you’re standing. Every pipe, pole and parcel your operation runs on, on one live map . Rank every candidate site by who’s within a five-minute drive . Get started for free Book a demo → Running on Felt Understand See your whole operation on one map Your asset records are in one system, your GIS data in another, and field reports in a third. Felt puts them on one map, so you can see what’s happening without switching between tools. Watch the full video Close ✕ Cloud Sources Live data, from wherever it lives Connect a database once and every map built on it stays current. Don’t run one? A Felt Server stores your raster and vector data for you, with permissions and live editing built in. Amazon S3 BigQuery Databricks ESRI Google Cloud Microsoft Azure MS SQL Postgres Snowflake STAC WFS WMTS Felt AI GIS expertise, a prompt away. Anyone on your team can ask which lines cross high fire hazard ground. Felt AI finds the hazard data, runs the analysis, and answers on the map, so crews know where to start. Anyone on your team can ask which sites sit in the 100-year floodplain. Felt AI finds FEMA’s flood zones, joins them to your locations, and answers on a map you can act on. Anyone on your team can ask which crew to send. Felt AI finds your crews, routes each one on the roads, and answers on the map. The closest isn’t always the quickest. Felt AI → Felt AI examples Fire season Ojai Valley, CA High water Cedar Rapids, IA Who to send Ashokan Reservoir, NY North canyon tap Miles in zone 1.0 Hazard zone Very High Poles 11 Last cleared 2022 Vegetation Management Which of our lines run through very high fire hazard zones? Found 1 layer · CAL FIRE Fire Hazard Severity Zones › Intersected 3 lines, 6.8 mi, with Very High zones › Cut 2 stretches in the zone · 18 poles › Lines in Very High Zones is live. Clear the north canyon first. It holds 11 of the 18 poles in Very High zones. In all, 1.7 of your 6.8 miles of line cross them. Enter prompt Site 07 · Warehouse Flood zone AE Annual chance 1 % Floor area 42,000 sq ft Source FEMA NFHL Site flood exposure Which of our sites are in the 100-year floodplain? Found 1 layer · FEMA National Flood Hazard Layer › Kept the 1% annual-chance zones · A, AE › Joined 13 sites to flood zones › Sites in the 100-year floodplain is live. 4 of your 13 sites are in it. All four are in zone AE on the river’s low banks, from Time Check to Czech Village. Enter prompt 2.3 km Crew 1 · 9 min Crew 2 · 3 min Crew 3 · 9 min Crew 4 · 5 min Line down Outage response A line’s down on Route 28 by the reservoir. Who should we send? Added crew locations · 4 points › Routed 4 crews on OpenStreetMap roads › Ranked 4 crews by drive time › Fastest crew route is live. Send Crew 2, 3 minutes out on Route 28. Crew 1 is closer as the crow flies, 2.3 km, but it’s across the reservoir: 9 minutes by road. Enter prompt Analysis Gain GIS superpowers Raster analysis, SQL, and spatial analysis used to take specialized desktop software and an afternoon. With Felt, they take a few clicks or an AI prompt, all in the browser. Web GIS → 01 Geocoding Drop in a spreadsheet of up to 10,000 addresses. Felt puts every one on the map. 02 Ready-made data Census, boundaries, flood risk, and infrastructure layers, ready to add to any map. 03 Drive-time areas Ask Felt AI who lives within a 20-minute drive of any site. 04 H3 hexagons Turn millions of points into clear hotspots of demand, activity, or risk. 05 Spatial analysis Buffer, clip, intersect, and count points in polygons, with no code. 06 Print layouts Client-ready pages with your logo, legend, scale bar, and north arrow. 07 GIS exports Take your data back out as GeoPackage, Shapefile, GeoJSON, or CSV. 08 Real-time collaboration Edit the same map together and see each other’s changes as they happen. Field App Close the loop between the field and the office Send crews out with the maps and forms they need, even offline. Felt’s iOS and Android app puts every inspection, photo and note they record back on the shared map, so the office can act on it the same day. Explore the Field App → For developers Build your business logic into Felt Felt makes it easy to build custom apps and workflows. Skip standing up tile servers or writing rendering code, and focus on what’s specific to your work. Embed maps with the JavaScript SDK, automate from Python or the REST API, and respond to changes with webhooks. App Development → Collaboration Share maps with clients, teams, and the public Send a link, or embed a live map on your website. Clients and colleagues view and comment without a seat, and nobody needs GIS training to explore the map. Web GIS → Customer stories Teams that run on Felt All customer stories → With Felt and Databricks, our site acquisition team was able to self-serve insights for the first time. Fastned Kenny Ling, Head of Location Intelligence How Fastned Uses Felt & Databricks to Build the Charging Network of Tomorrow Felt saves us hours on every analysis and has enabled us to build faster without increasing team size. Leaf Agriculture Alex Wimbush, VP of Product How Leaf unlocks cross-field agricultural analysis with Felt I find Felt the quickest and easiest way to have planners and analysts visualize data. Toole Design Group Joanna Wang, Planner and Data Analyst How Toole Transformed Transportation Planning with Interactive Geospatial Collaboration Industries See how teams like yours use Felt Agriculture → Verify on-farm practices and track every field in a program Cities and Government → Coordinate departments and publish maps for residents Climate and Natural Resources → Run field surveys and monitor change across your sites Education → Free maps for teaching and student projects Energy and Utilities → Screen sites, track leases, and inspect assets in the field Engineering and Infrastructure → Bring CAD, drone, and survey data together for client review Geospatial Analytics → Stream imagery and deliver maps and apps to clients Insurance → See which properties sit in flood and wildfire zones Real Estate → Screen sites and track every deal on its parcel Retail → Pick your next site and see how every store performs Telecom → Plan the next build and keep field crews in sync Transportation → Plan transit service and analyze fleet GPS data at scale Security You own your data, and it stays secure 01 SOC 2 Type 2 and GDPR Felt is SOC 2 Type 2 and GDPR compliant, with data encrypted in transit and at rest. The SOC 2 report is available on request. How Felt protects your data → 02 Hosting in your region Host your workspace in the US, EU, UK, Canada, or Australia, or run Felt in your own AWS account on the Enterprise plan. Hosting options → 03 Access you control Choose who can view, comment on, or edit each project, map, and data source, and enforce SSO on the Enterprise plan. Permissions and SSO → Map Gallery See how people around the world are mapping with Felt All maps in the gallery → Cities and government Business Development Opportunity Areas Explore sites suited for commercial, mixed-use, industrial, and office development in incentive zones. Geospatial analytics Damaged Building Detection Combine ground assessments with satellite-based SAR imagery for comprehensive impact analysis. Transportation Citi Bike Mobility Patterns Visualize demand hotspots, evaluate bike lane coverage, and plan for smarter micromobility infrastructure. Energy and utilities Wildfire Risk Assessment Evaluate fire risk zones and critical energy infrastructure for strategic decision-making in vulnerable areas. Energy and utilities Solar Site Suitability Explore proposed BLM solar development areas and assess site viability. Climate and natural resources Deforestation Monitoring Forest loss near Novo Progresso, Brazil reveals how roads drive Amazon deforestation patterns over 22 years. FAQ Common questions 01 Can Felt replace ArcGIS? Yes. Teams run their maps, analysis, dashboards, and field data collection on Felt with no Esri license. If you use ArcGIS today, Felt connects to your services and files, so you can move over all at once or one team at a time. See how Felt compares with ArcGIS . 02 Does Felt come with data, or do I bring my own? Both. The Global Library has ready-to-use layers, from boundaries and demographics to flood risk, roads, and buildings, and you add your own files, databases, and live links on top. 03 What data can I bring? Almost any spatial file, including Shapefiles, GeoJSON, GeoPackages, KML, File Geodatabases, and GeoTIFFs, up to 100 GB each. Upload a spreadsheet of addresses and Felt geocodes it, or connect a database or a Google Sheet that stays up to date. 04 Can I share maps outside my team? Yes. Send a link that opens without a login, invite clients to view and comment for free, or embed a map on your website. 05 Is Felt secure enough for sensitive data? Felt is SOC 2 Type 2 and GDPR compliant, and new maps are private until you share them. Enterprise adds SSO and regional hosting. See the security page . Try Felt Bring your data, see it on the map Connect a database or drop in a file and see your data live on a map in minutes. Get started for free Book a demo →",
