        "evidenceText": "Environmental Peacebuilding Association - Home   Welcome to the Environmental Peacebuilding Knowledge Platform This site serves both as the home page for the Environmental Peacebuilding Association® (also known as EnPAx®), and as a repository for a wide range of information on environmental peacebuilding. Environmental peacebuilding integrates natural resource management in conflict prevention, mitigation, resolution, and recovery to build resilience in communities affected by conflict. Join our growing global community of researchers, practitioners, and decision makers in sharing experiences and lessons from managing natural resources in conflict-affected settings, accessing new research on the topic, and participating in events to support the growing network of professionals active in environmental peacebuilding. Topics Assessment Basic Services Climate Change Conflict Causes Conflict Prevention Cooperation Data and Technologies Disasters Dispute Resolution/Mediation Economic Recovery Extractive Resources Gender Governance Humanitarian Assistance Land Livelihoods Peace Agreements Peace and Security Operations Programming Public Health Renewable Resources Weapons, Waste, and Pollution Recent Library Additions The Climate–Care Nexus: Addressing the Linkages Between Climate Change and Women’s and Girls’ Unpaid Care, Domestic, and Communal Work 2026 Climate, Peace and Security Fact Sheet: Somalia 2026 | Norwegian Institute of International Affairs and the Stockholm International Peace Research Institute Climate Security and Environmental Resilience in Afghanistan 2026 | Global Resilience NATO and the Environment 2026 | Environmental Law Reporter Community Seed Banks Deliver Social Cohesion and Peacebuilding in Conflict-Affected, Climate-Vulnerable Agricultural Contexts: A Study from Northern Ethiopia 2026 | CGIAR Join the Association Explore member benefits and opportunities to engage. Biweekly Newsletter News, jobs, and materials from the field. Environment and Security Peer-reviewed journal on environment, conflict, and peace. Events World Conference on Women's Empowerment, Gender Equity, and Social Impact Nov 12, 2026 | Scientific Research Conferences \"Talking Peace\" Dialogue Series: Energy, Conservation and Climate Adaptation Projects: Infrastructures for Peace or Conflict Drivers? Nov 12, 2026 | Bonn International Centre for Conflict Studies, RPTU Friedensakademie, and UNU Institute for Environment and Human Security COP31 Side Event | The Climate Costs of Military Spending: Emissions, Minerals and Diverted Finance Nov 14, 2026 | Conflict and Environment Observatory News Germany (with remote options): Research Interns on Environmental Peacebuilding Nov 10, 2026 | PRIF: Leibniz Peace Research Institute Frankfurt Venezuela: Official WASH Shelter & Infrastructure - Carupano Nov 9, 2026 | Danish Refugee Council Myanmar: Deputy Country Director Operations & Partnership (M/F) - Yangon Nov 9, 2026 | Solidarités International",
