      "audit": {
        "checkedAt": "2026-11-10T20:02:55.377Z",
        "httpStatus": 200,
        "finalUrl": "https://push-conference.com/",
        "contentType": "text/html; charset=utf-8",
        "pageTitle": "PUSH UX 2026 • UX &amp; Design Conference, Munich",
        "pageDescription": "One of Europe&#x27;s leading UX conferences 2026: a design conference for senior UX & product pros. 22–23 October, Munich — speakers from Berlin, London, Amsterdam & Zurich.",
        "evidenceText": "PUSH UX 2026 • UX & Design Conference, Munich The UX & Product conference for experienced professionals in the heart of Europe. 22–23 October 2026 Live in Munich Shaping UX since 2012 PUSH UX 2026 — The UX & Product conference for experienced professionals PUSH PUSH Tickets from €649 +VAT → See headliners 2026 partners: The event Professional growth that won’t feel like work. “The curation, the audience, and the overall vibe of the conference are unmatched.” Taras on PUSH 2025 · via LinkedIn PUSH UX 2026 in numbers 2 Conference days 16 Keynote sessions 28 Breakout sessions 700 Professionals The program A Europe-forward lineup of true makers & leaders. 🇺🇸 Chelsea Larsson Head of Content Design · Anthropic 🇬🇧 Dalia El-Shimy Director of UX Research · Wise 🇳🇱 Paulo Oliveira Global Innovation & Technology Manager · IKEA 🇩🇪 Julia Bastian Product Lead AI · Alasco 🇺🇸 Whitney Lacey Head of Content Design · Expedia Group 🇨🇭 Kris Hedstrom Head of UX Design & Research · On 🇪🇸 Angela Pesta Chief Design Officer · bsport 🇩🇪 Jake Ranallo Senior Product Designer · n8n 🇬🇧 Paavan Buddhdev Product Designer · Granola 🇩🇪 Bastian Gierull CEO Germany · Octopus Energy 🇫🇷 Karen Kaushansky Conversational AI Lead · Doctolib 🇩🇪 Oliver Dürr / Peer Langermann Interim UX Consultant / UX Manager · Leadium 🇳🇱 Natalia Marmolejo Design Lead · Rabobank 🇪🇸 Jason Giles VP Customer Intelligence · UserTesting 🇩🇪 Kevin Cannon Design Director · Superhuman And many more: Full program → Testimonials An outstanding event shaping UX since 2012: “I’ve not experienced an event as intense and important in almost 20 years.” Thomas on PUSH 2024 · via LinkedIn “The curation, the audience, and the overall vibe of the conference are unmatched.” Taras on PUSH 2025 · via LinkedIn “This felt like a hidden gem. Great content, super org and an awesome vibe.” Thomas, CSO on PUSH 2025 · via LinkedIn Conference venue Learn and network in a venue with personality. View 01 Main stage Alte Kongresshalle The Alte Kongresshalle (\"old congress center\") in Munich has been the home of PUSH UX for over a decade now. Built as a mid-century original in retro-futuristic style, it is now the charming backdrop for talks and exchange on UX, product and innovation. It's human, friendly, and adapts to change – just like we aim to do. Address Am Bavariapark 14 80339 Munich From central station U4/U5 subway · 15 min From airport S1/S8 train to central station + subway · 60 min Location details → Stay in the loop with the newsletter Never miss ticket drops or program updates . Email address Keep me posted This is the part of the page where you buy the ticket. If you've read this far you probably like what you saw. We like you too. Get your ticket → Frequently Asked Questions Why is PUSH UX conference considered an excellent event to attend? PUSH UX is active since 2012 and one of central Europe's longest-running UX design conferences. Fourteen years are proof of the continued quality and relevance , as few other events manage to exist for that long. PUSH UX has earned the trust of the UX community, and of top speakers from leading product companies such as Anthropic, Wise, Google, IDEO, BMW, UserTesting, Zalando, Granola and more. What makes this a UX conference for experienced professionals? The programme is curated specifically for advanced, honest, and highly practical content. You'll learn from the Head of Content Design at Anthropic, Director of UX Research at Wise, Head of AI Product Design at Zalando, Head of UX Design & Research at On, Chief Design Officer at bsport, VP Customer Intelligence at UserTesting and CEO Germany at Octopus Energy. The audience matches that level: around 80% of attendees are senior, lead, manager or director level. How does PUSH UX compare to UX conferences in Berlin, London or Amsterdam? Many people searching for a UX conference in Berlin, London, Amsterdam, Vienna or Zurich end up at PUSH UX, because the lineup is drawn from exactly those cities: several 2026 speakers join from Berlin and London, alongside Amsterdam, Zurich and Milan. You get the full European product scene in one place, in English, without a programme diluted by beginner tracks — and Munich is a short flight or train ride from all of them. Who attends PUSH UX? Around 700 attendees each year — mid-level to senior Product Designers, UX Researchers, Design Leaders, Product Managers and Engineers. Across recent years, roughly 60% attend at senior level, 20% as leads to directors, and 20% at mid level or below. Most travel in from Germany, Austria, the UK, the Netherlands, Norway, Denmark, Italy, Belgium and Poland — including strong contingents from Berlin, London, Amsterdam, Vienna and Zurich — working in European product companies, agencies and in-house design teams. Is PUSH UX a UX conference in Germany or an international event? Both. PUSH UX is hosted in Munich, Germany, and the entire programme is in English. Speakers in 2026 come from Germany, the UK, Switzerland, the Netherlands, France, Italy and the United States, which makes it a practical choice whether you are searching for a UX conference in Germany or a European UX event to travel to. Which UX conference in Europe should experienced professionals attend in 2026? PUSH UX 2026 is a UX Design & Product conference in the heart of Europe, built for experienced practitioners rather than beginners. It runs 22–23 October 2026 in Munich, Germany, and brings together ~700 senior Product Designers, UX Leaders, Researchers, PMs and Engineers for two days of talks, breakout sessions and workshops. If you are comparing UX conferences 2026 across Europe, it is one of the few design conferences aimed squarely at senior practice. When and where does the 2026 UX conference take place? PUSH UX 2026 takes place on 22 and 23 October 2026 at Alte Kongresshalle, Am Bavariapark 14, 80339 Munich, Germany. Optional workshops run around the main conference days. Munich Airport and the city's central station connect the venue to the rest of Europe within a few hours, with direct flights and trains from Berlin, London, Amsterdam, Vienna and Zurich. How much do tickets cost and how do I book? Conference tickets are €649 +VAT at the regular rate, and can be booked directly online. Prices increase in stages as the event approaches. Teams save up to 10% with group discounts. Combo tickets for the workshop day plus the main conference offer savings of €100 or more.",
