        "evidenceText": "11th Future Technologies Conference 2026 - Berlin | Converging AI, Quantum, Robotics, Cybersecurity, and Beyond Skip to main content 15-16 October 2026 · NYX Hotel Berlin Köpenick, Berlin, Germany 11 th Future Technologies Conference 2026 15-16 October 2026 in Berlin, Germany Call for Papers Register Now Watch video 11th Edition 60+ Countries represented 25 Published proceedings 10 Past editions online About the Future Technologies Conference Converging AI, Quantum, Robotics, Cybersecurity, and Beyond The Future Technologies Conference (FTC) has run annually since 2016, now marking its 11th edition, bringing together researchers, academics, and industry innovators to examine the technologies shaping the coming decade - from artificial intelligence and quantum computing to robotics, cybersecurity, and immersive systems. The conference provides a rigorous platform for peer-reviewed research, interdisciplinary exchange, and translating emerging ideas into practical impact through keynotes, technical sessions, and interactive discussions across academic and industrial domains. A decade in, FTC continues to shape the discourse on future technologies grounded in evidence, relevance, and societal need Call for Papers Register Now Host city Berlin NYX Hotel Berlin Köpenick Venue and travel Keynote talks Invited talks from leading researchers and practitioners in the field. Past speakers across SAI conferences have included researchers from Imperial College London, RWTH Aachen University, University of Amsterdam, University of Oxford, MIT, Stanford, Google, and Microsoft Research. Paper sessions Oral and poster presentations of peer-reviewed work. Virtual participation is available for authors unable to travel. Awards Outstanding papers and posters are recognised at the closing of the conference. Several award categories acknowledge distinguished contributions across research quality, innovation, and scholarly presentation. Networking Meet researchers and industry experts from 60+ countries across academia, research institutes, and industry. Selective peer review 37&ndash;39% acceptance rate across all conferences, reflecting double-blind review by an international programme committee. Co-located Events Held alongside 11th Future Technologies Conference 2026, sharing its dates, venue and proceedings. Future of Human-Computer Interaction Conference (FHCI) Learn more Future of Information and Computing Conference (FICC) Learn more Future of Intelligent and Autonomous Agents Conference (FIAA) Learn more Conference Tracks Choose the track that fits your research when you submit. Topic lists are indicative, and work across the field is welcome. Machine Learning 10 topics Deep Learning Agentic AI & Multi-Agent Systems Generative AI Explainable AI Large Language Models (LLMs) Computer Vision Reinforcement Learning Applied AI AI in Healthcare AI for Climate and Sustainability View track details Human-Computer Interaction 10 topics VR, AR, MR & XR Multimodal Interfaces Wearable Computing Brain Computer Interfaces Human-AI Co-Creativity Inclusive Design Context-Aware Computing Spatial Computing Voice & Conversational Interfaces Haptic & Physiological Interfaces View track details Data Science 10 topics Data Mining Predictive Modeling Data Analytics Data Fusion Sentiment Analysis Natural Language Processing Information Retrieval Big Data Speech Technologies AI Augmented Data Science View track details Cyber-Physical Systems 10 topics Smart Cities Smart Grids and Energy Networks Sensing and Sensor Networks Ambient Assisted Living Digital Twins Intelligent Transportation Smart Manufacturing Internet of Things (IoT) Autonomous Systems Geographic Information Systems View track details Future Computing Architectures 10 topics Quantum Computing Neuromorphic Systems High Performance Computing Human-Centered Computing Cloud Computing Edge and Fog Computing GPU Programming Distributed Computing Cognitive Systems Complex and Adaptive Systems View track details Robotics 10 topics Human Robot Interaction Cognitive Robotics Robotic Prosthetics Swarm Intelligence Real-Time Learning Self-Constructing Systems Bio-Inspired Robotics Continual Learning in Robotics Neuro-Robotic Interfaces Industry 5.0 View track details Cybersecurity 10 topics Cybersecurity Frameworks Threat Intelligence Cryptography Quantum-Resistant Security Internet and Cloud Security Digital Identity and Biometrics Trusted Architectures Privacy-Preserving AI Blockchain Ethical AI View track details Education Technology 10 topics AI in Education e-Learning Tools Gamified Learning Virtual Learning Ecosystems Social Learning Technologies Curriculum Design Learning Analytics Personalized Learning Accessibility and Inclusivity Delivery Systems and Environments View track details Your research, published and indexed Accepted papers appear in peer-reviewed conference proceedings. Publication partner The proceedings will be published by Springer in the \" Lecture Notes in Networks and Systems \" series. These proceedings will also be submitted for indexing in major databases, including Web of Science, SCOPUS, INSPEC, WTI Frankfurt eG, zbMATH, and SCImago. (*) Papers from the late-breaking round will be published as a separate proceedings volume after the conference. Submitted for indexing in WTI Frankfurt eG Springer LNNS series (opens in a new tab) Past proceedings Call for papers Proceedings Papers from past editions are published in proceedings by Springer. Choose a year to open its volumes on the publisher's website. 2025 Springer Volume 1 (opens in a new tab) Volume 2 (opens in a new tab) Volume 3 (opens in a new tab) Volume 4 (opens in a new tab) 2024 Springer Volume 1 (opens in a new tab) Volume 2 (opens in a new tab) Volume 3 (opens in a new tab) Volume 4 (opens in a new tab) 2023 Springer Volume 1 (opens in a new tab) Volume 2 (opens in a new tab) Volume 3 (opens in a new tab) Volume 4 (opens in a new tab) 2022 Springer Volume 1 