amme Committee, judged on originality, technical depth, impact and clarity. Read the full review process and criteria . What's the policy on AI-assisted writing tools? Generative AI may support drafting and language editing, but its use must be declared in the manuscript, it cannot be listed as an author, and authors stay fully accountable for the content. See the full AI policy . Do you support visa letters for travel? Yes - registered, presenting authors can request an invitation/visa support letter. Contact us via the Contact page once registered. What's your registration and refund policy? Registration Categories Author: Authors are those presenting a paper at the conference. Each author registration allows presentation of one paper only, and includes access to keynotes, paper sessions, and all conference activities. Participant: Participants are attendees who do not submit or present a paper but wish to attend presentations, keynotes, and sessions. Payment Information Registration fees must be paid in advance. We accept most major international credit and debit cards. Payments can also be made via bank transfer. If you wish to pay by bank transfer, please contact us at [email protected] to request an invoice with the necessary payment details. Registration Policy Each registration is valid for one delegate only. Each author registration permits the presentation of one paper. All registrations are final and non-refundable. Registrations are non-transferable to another delegate. What People Say &ldquo;What an exciting and intellectually stimulating day at the Future Technologies Conference (FTC) 2026 in Berlin!\r\n\r\nA particular highlight for me was the fantastic keynote.\r\nI also enjoyed the discussions on smart healthcare and the challenges of robotics and automation, as well as the fascinating conversations over coffee and the thoughtful questions after my presentation. It is always rewarding to discover unexpected connections between different fields of research.\r\nA day full of ideas, curiosity and inspiring exchanges!&rdquo; Ilona Negro European Personnel Selection Office Read Full Review &ldquo;It was actually great and completely different from what I expected—I thought it might be a bit like white noise, where you’d fall asleep or end up on your phone, but it was genuinely interesting and engaging because the speakers came with very challenging subjects. They really challenged you to think about them. I felt there was so much there that I could take away. I know I was always asking questions at the end, but that’s precisely because it was actually interesting. The talks constantly stimulated my thinking and made me think, “Okay, I hadn’t seen it that way before.”&rdquo; Adrian Neal Capgemini &ldquo;Beyond presenting my research and hearing great keynotes, I was impressed by how intentionally the organizers created chances to connect: small tasks, smart questions, simple prompts that sparked real conversations, and feel at home in a room full of new people.\r\n\r\nIt turned the conference into something rare:\r\nengaging, energizing, and genuinely community-building.&rdquo; Leonie Reichardt BMW Motorrad Read Full Review &ldquo;For me, it was super cool that there was a short track on digital health, which, of course, I enjoyed very much. But it was also a great experience to take a step back and get a broader view of what’s going on in AI and in completely different industries. AI is such an amazing and rapidly growing field that there’s always a danger of getting stuck in your own area of digital health, like in my case. So, it was really good to take inspiration from other areas and industries, including security and all of that.&rdquo; Jan Kirchhoff DigiHealth Institute of Hochschule Neu-Ulm &ldquo;It was rewarding to see the talk spark engaged questions and thoughtful discussion. The keynotes and many of the paper sessions were excellent — with AI unsurprisingly front and centre. I came away with a much clearer sense of where work on neural networks and deep learning is heading. Equally valuable were the conversations in between sessions, connecting with people from both academia and industry.&rdquo; Jakob Lütkemeier Trinity College Dublin &ldquo;I can confidently say that these events have always been a great source of knowledge and inspiration. I would like to thank the organisers for consistently delivering such top‑notch conferences that bring together brilliant minds and foster meaningful discussions. I look forward to continuing the conversations sparked during the event and to seeing how the ideas we explored will grow in the months ahead.&rdquo; Reno Yuri Camilleri University of Malta &ldquo;A special thank you to SAI Conferences for an inspiring and highly engaging event, and to all colleagues who joined the session, asked thoughtful questions, and exchanged ideas on the future of digital transformation in higher education.&rdquo; Tiago H. Moreira de Oliveira NOVA IMS Photos from 2025 Social media aggregator → Explore Other SAI Conferences Part of the SAI Conferences portfolio, spanning computing, AI, and emerging technologies. Computer Vision Conference 15-16 April 2027 Mercure Amsterdam City Hotel Netherlands Learn more Computing Conference 8-9 July 2027 Clayton Hotel Chiswick United Kingdom Learn more Intelligent Systems Conference 2-3 September 2027 Mercure Amsterdam City Hotel Netherlands Learn more",
