        "evidenceText": "IBCS Annual Conference 2026 • IBCS - International Business Communication Standards IBCS Annual Conference 2026 Coming home: The origin. The accomplishment. The next chapter. June 12, 2026 Steigenberger Inselhotel Konstanz, Germany June 11, 19:00 CEST (the evening before the conference) General Assembly of the IBCS Association Followed by a get-together. Don’t miss this evening networking event before the IBCS Annual Conference.   All members of the IBCS Association can join either on-site or online . June 12, 9:00 to 17:00 CEST IBCS Annual Conference 2026 The IBCS Annual Conference is an exclusive event for certified IBCS professionals , bringing together the best in business communication. Expect high-level discussions, fresh insights, and valuable networking opportunities. This year’s conference will not only decide on IBCS Version 2.0 and introduce ISO 24896 “Notation for business reporting”, but will also help shape the future of the IBCS community. AGENDA 9:00 Hello, welcome and IBCS news   Moderators: Johannes von Mulert , Board Member at IBCS Association Edyta Szarska, Managing Partner at IBCS Institute Presentations by new IBCS Certified Consultants : + Juliane Auer (MHP, Germany) + Marion Berg (consultnetwork, Germany) + Daniel Berthold (KEYE Advisory, Germany) + Michael Darnieder (TEDEXA, Germany) + Ömer Degirmenci (MHP, Germany) + Jürgen Gerner (SUSS, Germany) + Tomasz Glenszczyk (Capgemini, Poland) + Iwona Stasiak (Housea, Poland) + Grozdanka Ivanovska (INGENIUM, North Macedonia) + Ian Mercado (Dyflex Solutions, Australia) + Rodrigo Palomino CPA (Department of Energy and Economic Diversification, Australia) and new IBCS Certified Software from: + Farseer + Infotopics + Microsoft 9:45 Publication of ISO 24896 “Notation for business reporting”   Diego Berea , Managing Partner at Ozona Consulting ISO 20000-2 Co-Editor and ISO 24896 Project Leader Angelika Vaasa , Head of Quality Coordination Unit at European Parliament Convenor of ISO TC37/WG11 10:05 IBCS Study 2026 – final results   Arne-Kristian Schulz , Associate Partner at Blueforte Co-author and coordinator of the study 10:25 Mission accomplished + What is the impact of ISO 24896? + Will this lead to better report composition?   Jürgen Faisst , Managing Partner at IBCS Institute 10:45 Coffee . 11:15 “I am not happy with the reports I get” Better executive decision-making – A discussion using real boardroom cases.   Mario Laube , CEO at Erfurter Verkehrsbetriebe AG 11:35 Next chapter of IBCS     Stefanie Fröhner , Founder at DatenMenschen – Erfolg mit datAInsights Arne-Kristian Schulz , Associate Partner at Blueforte Bernie Smith , Founder at Made to Measure KPIs Edyta Szarska , Managing Partner at IBCS Institute 12:30 Lunch . 13:30 News from IBCS Sponsors   IBCS Platinum Sponsor 2026 Dipti Borkar , Vice President and General Manager at Microsoft IBCS Gold Sponsors 2026 Holger Gerths , Product Lead Financial Management at Corporate Planning Jie Deng , Product Manager, and Felix Müller , Lead for Design CC Planning & Analytics at SAP Geneve Schwan , Chief Product Officer at TRUECHART by HICO-Group Andrej Lapajne , Founder, and Richard Cooper , CEO at Zebra BI 14:30 Will AI power decision-making? Panel discussion: Challenging software vendors to meet the needs of executives Executives: Thomas Bodé , Chief Digital Transformation Officer at MET Group Former Vice President, Head of Data & Analytics at SWAROVSKI Renata Neidrowska , Interim CFO at Grupa Oryx C-level executive, Supervisory Board Member, ACCA Poland Panel Member Xavier Subirats , Partner at AMSEL ASSESSORS Member of Steering Committees/Boards of Directors, the Boards of the Catalan Economists Association (CEC) and the Association for Management Accountancy (ACCID) Jürgen Faisst , Managing Partner at IBCS Institute Former CEO of Thinking Networks AG, COO, CTO at MIS AG . . Moderator: Paul Damen , Co-Founder at Rockfeather . Software vendors: Holger Gerths , Product Lead Financial Management at Corporate Planning Michael Schwan , CEO at HICO-Group Liran Edelist , Chief Customer Officer at Lumel Dipti Borkar , Vice President and General Manager at Microsoft Andrej Lapajne , Founder at Zebra BI 15:00 Coffee . 15:30 AI-powered vs. human-centered composition Brainstorming session: How AI will shape the future roles of stakeholders in reporting Interlude: AI and/or humans creating UNIFORMCHARTs Rolf Hichert and Fernando Fragoso, UNIFORMCHART Presentation of round table conclusions   Round tables by stakeholders: + Investors, supervisory board members Moderator: Jens Ropers , Partner at CA Akademie + Executives, CXO Moderator: Markus Wolff , Co-Founder and Managing Director of chartisan + Analysts, controllers, FP&A Moderator: Simone Verza , freelance Consultant and Trainer + Consultants, BI professionals Moderator: Raphael Branger , Chairman of the Board of Directors at IT-Logix 16:30 Back to the origin To open IBCS’s next chapter, we return to where it all began: communicating successfully.   17:00 End of conference Apéro (get-together)   Moderator: Johannes von Mulert , Board Member at IBCS Association Special guest: Rolf Hichert , Former President of the IBCS Association Impressions Take a look at pictures from the conference. More ISO 24896 foundation and IBCS composition of compelling reports (public) IBCS Certified Analyst/Professional First stage of certification: Understand the SUCCESS formula of IBCS and learn how to apply it in practice. Followed by an online test for becoming an IBCS Certified Analyst/Professional. Classroom training takes two days, online training consist of four sessions of three and a half hours. View program and dates A special thanks to the IBCS 2026 sponsors: IBCS Platinum Sponsor Vendor of IBCS® Certified Software ‘Microsoft Fabric Planning’ More IBCS Gold Sponsors IBCS® Certified Software for Corporate Planner, Power BI, and Qlik More Vendor of IBCS® Certified Software ‘SAP Analytics Cloud’ More IBCS® Certified S