        "evidenceText": "Infographics | South China Morning Post Infographics + FOLLOW Hong Kong Tai Po fire report: lessons from a tragedy A judge-led inquiry into Hong Kong’s deadliest fire in decades has delivered a scathing report condemning the main renovation contractor and project consultant, while also criticising four government bodies for systemic oversight failures. Here is a look at some of the key findings. 31 Oct 2026 - 5:30PM SCMP Plus Going Global 100 8 Oct 2026 - 11:00AM China’s anti-corruption fight in numbers 25 Aug 2026 - 6:06AM Infographics Exercise, supplements, digital detoxing: Hongkongers’ new lifestyle obsessions In a city long known for its frenetic pace and high-stress work environment, residents are becoming increasingly health-conscious. 17 Aug 2026 - 12:50PM Hong Kong Unpacking Hong Kong's five-year plan and its role in China's development In a milestone moment, Hong Kong will unveil its first-ever five-year plan in September, aligning the city’s priorities with the nation’s 2026-2030 development blueprint. 12 Aug 2026 - 3:00PM World Infographic: a powerful new El Nino cycle begins. Is the world ready? Discover the history and science behind El Nino, the ‘Pacific fever’ that turbocharges extreme weather globally. 7 Aug 2026 - 5:25AM Advertisement Advertisement Advertisement Hong Kong What made Hong Kong's Tai Po fire so deadly? During the final round of hearings into Hong Kong’s deadliest inferno in decades, experts pointed to shortfalls that caused the Wang Fuk Court blaze to spread at an unprecedented rate. 14 Jul 2026 - 9:31AM Society Ageing in Hong Kong – should you fear it? Hong Kong is one of the fastest-ageing societies in the world. While this brings mounting challenges, it also creates growing opportunities. Here is what you need to know. 12 Jul 2026 - 12:55PM Science An immersive visual guide to China’s space station Explore the Tiangong space station and track its simulated orbit in our infographic. 23 Jun 2026 - 5:30PM Hong Kong A city remembers: the names of the 168 people who died in the Tai Po fire Hong Kong releases the names of the 168 victims of the Wang Fuk Court fire, as seven individuals face manslaughter charges. 11 Jun 2026 - 7:30AM Football A comprehensive visual guide to the 2026 Fifa World Cup Explore the beautiful game – now bigger, more competitive and expanded to 48 teams. 9 Jun 2026 - 9:00PM Health & Environment ‘Silent killer’: the race to beat cancer in Hong Kong Despite a rising number of cancer cases in Hong Kong, survival rates are improving. Here is what you need to know. 31 May 2026 - 9:00PM China A comprehensive visual guide to Trump’s 2026 state visit to China Go inside Donald Trump’s 43-hour whirlwind trip to Beijing through our complete visual breakdown. 16 May 2026 - 9:34AM China Handshakes of history: when Chinese and US leaders meet - an infographic Explore the meetings that have helped shape one of the world's most consequential bilateral relationships. 21 Sep 2026 - 5:16PM Hong Kong Residents passed from pillar to post as warnings before fatal Hong Kong fire went unheeded The third round of Wang Fuk Court fire hearings, held from April 20 to 30, exposed a “regulatory vacuum” in key areas that contributed to the high death toll, as departments said oversight lay elsewhere. 6 May 2026 - 8:32AM Hong Kong How fire safety failures worsened Hong Kong’s deadly inferno The second round of hearings from April 8 to April 17 exposed a series of failures that allowed the fire equipment and alarm system in Wang Fuk Court to be deactivated for months, and eventually contributed to the heavy death toll. 23 Apr 2026 - 6:04PM Sport Rugby’s greatest weekend: 50 years of the Hong Kong Sevens - an infographic See the world’s top teams compete at Kai Tak Stadium on April 17-19 and celebrate 50 years of Hong Kong Sevens history, tries and triumphs. 16 Apr 2026 - 8:15PM Advertisement Advertisement Advertisement China Interactive | Made in China 2025: Clearing the way for a 