        "evidenceText": "SkyTruth Tools Insights Impact Contact Donate Making environmental harm visible, measurable, and actionable SkyTruth is a conservation technology nonprofit that leverages satellite imagery and environmental data to create tools and develop insights that drive accountability, accelerate climate action, and support biodiversity protection. Generating impact for the planet We believe that generating impact requires innovation and collaboration. Since our founding in 2001, organizations around the world have used our tools and insights to promote conservation efforts and hold polluters accountable. We equip advocates, journalists, policymakers, and other changemakers with free, accessible tools and insights that advance efforts in: Revealing and eliminating marine pollution from ocean industries Powering the global movement to end fossil fuel dependence Accelerating global biodiversity protection Past Event: CBD COP 17 Leveraging Open Tools and Data in the Push for 30x30 SkyTruth hosted an event on Friday, October 30th at the Ocean Pavilion at CBD COP 17 to explore how free, open data and tools can help deliver 30x30 from designation into delivery. Read the event recap Past Event: Climate Week NYC Turning Geospatial Data into Action on Pollution and Climate SkyTruth convened environmental science, technology, philanthropy, and policy leaders to tackle a key question: ‍How can geospatial data accelerate progress on the planet's most pressing environmental challenges? Read the event recap Annual Report 2025 From Insight to Impact Open, trusted data driving policy and protection Read the Report Innovative tools that expose environmental issues We build powerful, open-source tools that turn satellite imagery and geospatial data into environmental insight. Combining advanced analytics with deep expertise in remote sensing, our tools bring to light human activities often hidden from view. Explore our Tools Cerulean The first free, publicly available technology that uses AI and satellite imagery to expose chronic ocean oil pollution and its potential sources. Exposes chronic oil pollution Empowers ocean advocates Reveals pollution hotspots Increases maritime accountability Learn more 30x30 Progress Tracker An interactive platform that tracks global, regional, and national progress towards conserving 30% of the planet by 2030. Tracks conservation progress Democratizes data Evaluates protection effectiveness Increases transparency Learn more Mining Tools and data revealing the environmental impacts of mountaintop mining. Learn more Flaring Maps displaying natural gas flaring worldwide to expose waste and emissions. Learn more Monitor An open platform for exploring satellite imagery and tracking environmental impacts worldwide. Learn more News and Insights View more Insights We turn data into clear, actionable understanding. By combining our tools with in-depth analysis, we reveal patterns, surface risks, and provide the clarity needed to drive smarter environmental decisions. 23 September 2026 Report Global Estimate of Marine Oil Pollution New global analysis estimates oil slicks cover 1.58 million km² of ocean surface each year. The report maps chronic oil pollution from vessels and offshore oil industry infrastructure, identifying where pollution is concentrated, which fleets are associated, and gaps in accountability. Read more Blog 21 September 2026 AI at SkyTruth: Staying Human-Centered Read more Blog 12 August 2026 Beyond 30x30: Measuring the Effectiveness of Protected Areas with TPARA Read more Newsletter 28 October 2026 SkyTruth in Focus: September/October 2026 Read more News 4 October 2026 An oil spill across the world's oceans covers an area three times larger than Thailand, with cargo ships and oil tankers identified as the main culprits. Read more News 2 October 2026 Satellite data reveal massive scale of routine oil pollution in oceans. See the map Read more Newsletter 25 August 2026 SkyTruth in Focus: