        "evidenceText": "EuroCarto 2026 EuroCarto2026 has come to an end. Thank you for being part of it! From September 8–11, 2026 , Brno became a meeting place for the European and international cartographic community. More than 260 participants came together for four days of presentations, keynote lectures, workshops, poster sessions, discussions, and networking. Under the motto “Let’s transform cartography together” , EuroCarto 2026 provided a platform for researchers, professionals, and students to exchange ideas, share new developments, and discuss the future of cartography, geovisualization, and spatial technologies. The conference began on Tuesday, September 8, with pre-conference workshops , followed by the Opening Ceremony and Welcome Reception in the evening. The main scientific programme continued from Wednesday to Friday at Masaryk University. Organized by the Czech Cartographic Society under the patronage of the International Cartographic Association , EuroCarto 2026 welcomed participants from across Europe and beyond, bringing together a diverse community with a shared interest in the transformation and future of cartography. Thank you to everyone who joined us in Brno and helped make these four days of cartography, exchange, and inspiration possible! Video daily highlights / EuroCarto 2026 A days worth replaying. The moments that made EuroCarto 2026. Were you there? EuroCarto 2026 / Daily highlights EuroCarto, day by day. Loading video… This video could not be loaded. Try again Day 4 highlights Fri, 11 Sep Day 4 Latest Fri, 11 Sep Day 3 Thu, 10 Sep Day 2 Wed, 9 Sep Day 1 Tue, 8 Sep EuroCarto 2026 / Photo diary Four days. Countless moments. View all photos ↗ ↗ ↗ ↗ ↗ ↗ ↗ ↗ ↗ ↗ ↗ ↗ ↗ ↗ ↗ ↗ ↗ ↗ ↗ ← → Good company. Great memories. EuroCarto 2026 / Photo diary A little closer. ✕ ← Unable to load this photo. Open the original → From the community / LinkedIn The conversation continues. Different perspectives. One cartographic community. ← → Drag to browse Op