        "evidenceText": "Home - Investigative Reporters and Editors Skip to content Three journalists of color named IRE’s 2027 Chauncey Bailey Fellows, carrying his investigative legacy forward October 20, 2026 Read More Chronicling capture: how investigative journalism covers private actors usurping public institutions October 19, 2026 Read More IRE announces newly-revised Code of Conduct: A commitment to inclusion, safety and community October 15, 2026 Read More IRE announces $25K donation from late executive director October 12, 2026 Read More IRE recognized as a champion of ‘preserving local news online’ with the 2026 Internet Archive Hero Award October 5, 2026 Read More Welcome to IRE! Investigative Reporters and Editors Inc. is a grassroots nonprofit organization dedicated to improving the quality of investigative reporting. IRE was formed to create a forum in which journalists throughout the world could help each other by sharing story ideas, newsgathering techniques and news sources. IRE provides members access to thousands of reporting tipsheets and other materials through its Resource Center and hosts conferences and specialized training across the country. Programs of IRE include the National Institute for Computer-Assisted Reporting (NICAR), a collaboration between IRE and the Missouri School of Journalism. Upcoming events Loading ... Training Opportunities Learn the latest techniques of finding, understanding and reporting on stories with IRE. Explore training options across the globe and find an event that fits your schedule, whether it’s in person or online. View Calendar IRE News Three journalists of color named IRE’s 2027 Chauncey Bailey Fellows, carrying his investigative legacy forward October 20, 2026 | Comments Off on Three journalists of color named IRE’s 2027 Chauncey Bailey Fellows, carrying his investigative legacy forward October 20, 2026 — Chauncey Bailey would have turned 77 today. Nineteen years after he was killed while reporting an investigative story in Oakland, Ca., IRE is marking his birthday for the first time by announcing the newest class of the fellowship that bears his name, a choice meant to keep his work and legacy&hellip; IRE announces newly-revised Code of Conduct: A commitment to inclusion, safety and community October 15, 2026 | Comments Off on IRE announces newly-revised Code of Conduct: A commitment to inclusion, safety and community October 15, 2026 – The Investigative Reporters and Editors (IRE) Board of Directors has approved a newly-revised Code of Conduct, a pivotal step toward fostering a more inclusive and safe environment for all members and participants. “Everyone is welcome at IRE events, and it’s important that they feel included and supported while in attendance,” said&hellip; IRE announces $25K donation from late executive director October 12, 2026 | Comments Off on IRE announces $25K donation from late executive director IRE is honored and touched to announce that Diana Fuentes, IRE’s late executive director, has generously donated $25,000 to the organization upon her passing. 1 2 3 &hellip; 358 Next &raquo; There’s more pressure than ever to rise above the competition.   IRE can help you enhance your daily reporting with resources and member benefits you won’t find anywhere else. Become a Member &times; Year-end giving Keep the watchdogs watching. Give before December 31st to train and support thousands of journalists holding the powerful accountable. Donate now Don&rsquo;t show this again Maybe later IRE year-end giving modal lives here (hidden in the editor). Preview on the live page with ?ire_eoy_preview=1 . Scroll To Top",
