        "pageTitle": "Power BI - Data Visualization | Microsoft Power Platform",
        "pageDescription": "Microsoft Power BI is a business intelligence platform that helps you visualize data and infuse insights into your existing Microsoft 365 apps. Try it for free.",
        "evidenceText": "Power BI - Data Visualization | Microsoft Power Platform This is the Trace Id: 755c4b6bd684e21020c63e00b9276dcb Skip to main content Microsoft Fabric Power BI Product features overview Power BI Desktop Pro Premium Embedded Report Server Microsoft Fabric IQ Fabric Data Factory Fabric Data Engineering Fabric Data Warehousing Fabric Real-Time Intelligence Fabric Data Science Fabric Databases Microsoft OneLake Security and governance Managed application backend Pricing Partners Documentation Data 101 Data Storytelling Power BI Blog Power BI Support Power BI Community Power BI Downloads Migrate Buy now Start free Sign in Discover what's coming to Microsoft Ignite, Nov 17-20, 2026. Register now Power BI</h1> \"> Power BI Uncover powerful insights and turn them into impact with a unified analytics platform. Visualize any data and use Copilot in Microsoft Fabric to quickly explore, explain, and take action. Try for free Product overview Create a data-driven culture with business intelligence for all</h2> \"> Create a data-driven culture with business intelligence for all Power BI features Copilot in Microsoft Fabric Power BI in Microsoft Fabric Building agentic apps Previous Next Make fast, informed enterprise decisions Connect governed data, trusted metrics, and interactive insights into one enterprise decision layer—so all your teams can make confident decisions, faster. Take a guided tour Connect and unify all your data Seamlessly connect to data from any source, cloud or on-premises, and bring it together in one place with OneLake to create a single source of truth for your organization. Learn more Drive impact with self-service BI for everyone Give all your people access to an intuitive, easy-to-use business intelligence experience for any skill level—whether they’re­ analysts, decision-makers, or new team members. Learn more Empower every data team with AI-driven insights Reshape how your organization accesses, manages, and acts on data by activating Microsoft Fabric in your Power BI experience. Learn more From question to insight, without the manual work Ask questions about your data or describe the report you need in natural language, and Copilot handles the rest — pulling the right data and generating visualizations and reports automatically, without manual report building. Learn more Get fast AI-generated insights and narratives Use Copilot to generate instant text summaries and easy-to-understand narratives to quickly identify key trends in your data. For example, ask Copilot to add a summary to a dashboard that highlights why sales spiked this quarter—turning raw numbers into meaningful takeaways. Learn more Boost creator productivity Accelerate analytics by turning complex data modeling into a guided, AI-assisted experience—so teams can build trusted, business-ready semantic models faster and with fewer bottlenecks. Learn more Overview Enable users without paid licenses to interact with reports and access the rest of your Microsoft Fabric workloads. Learn more Build a unified analytics ecosystem Extend Power BI beyond dashboards by connecting directly to Microsoft Fabric, enabling faster end-to-end insights, from ingestion to visualization. Learn more Strengthen security and governance with OneLake Get consistent security, governance, and trusted data across every report and dataset with OneLake, which provides a centralized data foundation with open formats. Learn more Democratize access efficiently Scale access, simplify administration, and optimize costs while delivering governed insights to every user with a unified capacity model from Fabric. Learn more Do more than ever with Power BI Discover a modern way of dashboarding with interactive, agentic applications, you can create using natural language. Read the blog post Build on data you already trust Create apps directly on Power BI semantic models, so every experience is grounded in your organization's governed data, trusted metrics, and business logic. Learn more Move from insight to action Go beyond exploring data by building interactive experiences that help users make decisions, trigger workflows and take actions. Browse the App Gallery Back to tabs Use cases See what you can do with Power BI</h2> \"> See what you can do with Power BI Build trusted semantic data models Ensure every report and AI interaction is grounded in trusted business logic with enterprise-grade semantic models from Power BI. Tell a story with powerful visuals Turn your data into interactive visuals that help make insights immediately clear, comparable, and actionable. Get quick answers from Copilot Ask Copilot questions, get trusted answers, and explore insights using AI grounded in your business data. Connect insights to your workflows Share insights securely across Microsoft Teams, PowerPoint, SharePoint, and other apps your people use every day. Turn insights into action Trigger workflows, update data, and drive outcomes directly from your analytics to make an impact. Embed BI reports for your customers Improve usability and user engagement in your own apps by using Power BI Embedded to deliver stunning reports. Previous Slide Next Slide Establish a governed source of truth</h4> \"> Establish a governed source of truth Organize your data, control access, reduce duplication, enable a data mesh, endorse datasets, and search in OneLake. Learn more Unify enterprise scale and self service</h4> \"> Unify enterprise scale and self service Drive insights and innovation at every level, informally among teams and formally curated and distributed by IT. Learn more Infuse data experiences everywhere</h4> \"> Infuse data experiences everywhere Gain interoperation with the apps people already use, such as Microsoft Teams, Microsoft 365, and Dynamics 365. Learn more Empower anyone to work with data</h4> \"> Empower anyone to work with data Foster a data-driven culture with free training and a familiar interface built to work with assistive technology. See training resources Get started immediately</h4> \"> Get started immediately Simplify report building with a drag-and-drop canvas, AI that can auto-generate reports, and hundreds of template apps. Browse apps Embed BI reports for your customers</h4> \"> Embed BI reports for your customers Reduce time to market by customizing, extending, and incorporating BI into your apps and branding them as your own. Learn more Back to Modal section RESEARCH AND NEWS Independent research and news</h2> \"> Independent research and news Previous tab Next tab Microsoft was positioned as A Leader in Gartner® Magic Quadrant™ for Analytics and Business Intelligence Platforms 2026. 2 Read the report Read about the latest Power BI innovations. Read the blog Back to tabs Pricing Plans to suit every need</h2> \"> Plans to suit every need See pricing details Free account Create rich, interactive reports with visual analytics at your fingertips for free. Free Start free Power BI Pro Access Power BI reports shared with you and publish your own for an even bigger impact. $14.00 user/month, paid yearly Buy now Power BI Premium Per User License specific users with enterprise-scale features. $24.00 user/month, paid yearly Buy now Power BI in Microsoft Fabric Share reports with users who don’t have paid licenses and get access to Microsoft Fabric workloads using a single capacity. Variable See pricing Security Gain visibility into your data estate</h2> \"> Gain visibility into your data estate Get peace of mind with built-in security features and interoperation with leading security and governance solutions. Explore security features Customer stories Real customers, real results</h2> \"> Real customers, real results Previous Slide Next Slide “In the last year alone, we’ve eliminated almost 10,000 manual hours through Microsoft-powered automation. That’s time we now spend creating business value.” Jerod Ridge, Director of Data Engineering, Lumen Read the story View all stories “We can slice and dice the data to get practically any piece of information instantaneously. Power BI gives us the agility to present data in a compelling and interesting way.” Andy Whitby, Assistant Territorial Property Director, The Salvation Army UK Read the story View all stories “At Walmart, we use a myriad of different vendors in our technology stack, so having a tool like Power BI that can bring everything together was critical.” Micah Dail, Director, Finance Data & Analytics, Walmart Read the story View all stories ”Our PowerBot agent has boosted efficiency and generated higher-quality proposals in a short timeframe.” Sabine van Woerden, Director, Legal Innovation, HEINEKEN 3.1 million Hours in increased productivity Read the story View all stories Back to CUSTOMER STORIES section Resources Explore everything Power BI has to offer</h2> \"> Explore everything Power BI has to offer Getting started Training Help Previous Next Previous Slide Next Slide Get started with Power BI</h3> \"> Free trial Get started with Power BI Find insights within your data and share rich analytics reports. Try it for free Get Power BI Desktop</h3> \"> Desktop app Get Power BI Desktop Create rich, interactive reports with visual analytics at your fingertips. Get it for free Get the mobile app</h3> \"> Mobile app Get the mobile app Securely access and view live Power BI dashboards and reports on any device, with native mobile apps for Windows, iOS, and Android. Get it for free Try Power BI Report Server</h3> \"> On premises Try Power BI Report Server Get a free trial of the on-premises solution for reporting with the flexibility to move to the cloud. Try it for free Back to Resources - Getting started tab section Previous Slide Next Slide Learn how to use Power BI</h3> \"> Courses Learn how to use Power BI Take hands-on guided learning courses to help you meet your goals quickly, gain confidence, and learn at your own pace. See training collections Read technical documentation</h3> \"> Documentation Read technical documentation Get expert information and answers to address your needs, no matter how you use Power BI. Browse documentation Read the Power BI Blog</h3> \"> Blog Read the Power BI Blog Get the latest news, feature updates, and product announcements. Read the blog Back to resources - learning tab section Previous Slide Next Slide Get Power BI and Microsoft Fabric support</h3> \"> Support Get Power BI and Microsoft Fabric support Check service status and get technical support for Power BI in Microsoft Fabric. Get support Get expert support and tips</h3> \"> Community Get expert support and tips Discover useful tips and advice from the Power BI team by connecting with Power BI community members around the world. Join the community Back to resources - help tab section Back to tabs Frequently asked questions Expand all Collapse all 01/ What is Power BI and what’s it used for? Power BI is a unified, scalable platform for self-service and enterprise business intelligence (BI). You can use it to connect to and visualize any data, and infuse the visuals into the apps you use every day. 02/ What is a business intelligence platform? A business intelligence platform is a tool that connects, analyzes, and visualizes data so organizations can make better decisions. With Power BI, this means turning your data into interactive dashboards and insights that help teams understand performance and take action faster. 03/ How should I choose a Power BI license for my organization? Power BI licenses aren’t exclusive—there are several ways to mix and match plans and licenses. For example, you could purchase Premium (P-SKU) or Microsoft Fabric (F-SKU) capacity to host the most popular reports, and then buy Power BI Pro licenses (or get them through Microsoft 365 E5) for your users who need to create and publish reports. Contact a sales expert to learn more. Contact sales 04/ What is Power BI Embedded? Microsoft Power BI Embedded is a pay-as-you-go platform as a service (PaaS) offering. It allows app developers to embed fully interactive reports into their apps without having to build their own data visuals and controls. Power BI Embedded costs as little as $1 per hour for analytics, with no requirement for end-user licensing. Try Power BI Embedded 05/ What’s the difference between Microsoft Fabric and Power BI? Microsoft Fabric is an end-to-end analytics solution with full-service capabilities including data movement, data lakes, data engineering, data integration, data science, real-time analytics, data monitoring, and business intelligence—all backed by a shared platform providing robust data security, governance, and compliance. Power BI provides the business intelligence layer in Microsoft Fabric that enables you to gain insights from your data. Power BI Premium customers can simply turn on the Fabric tenant setting and access the rest of the product in a unified experience. And with its unified capacity model, Power BI Premium per capacity can be used against any Microsoft Fabric workload. 06/ Can I access Microsoft Fabric if I'm a Power BI Pro customer? Power BI Pro customers can access Fabric workloads only through the Microsoft Fabric trial experience. Try Microsoft Fabric 07/ What features are available in Fabric SKUs compared to Power BI SKUs? Feature availability depends on both SKU and capacity level. See the features list for specific details. 08/ Are there free Power BI training and certifications available for my team? Yes, Microsoft offers free, self-paced Power BI training through Microsoft Learn, with structured learning paths that cover everything from getting started to building reports and modeling data. You can also take practice assessments to prepare for official certifications once your team is ready. Explore learning paths 09/ What are some Power BI dashboard examples? Microsoft provides a wide range of Power BI dashboard examples to help you get started. On Microsoft Learn, you can explore and downl