        "pageDescription": "Selenium is a browser automation tool that gives you full control over Chrome, Firefox, Edge and Safari. Write your scripts in Java, Python, C#, Ruby, JavaScript or Kotlin using the official W3C WebDriver standard.",
        "evidenceText": "Selenium For AI agents: the site's llms.txt is at /llms.txt. Automate any browser, from any language. Selenium is a browser automation tool that gives you full control over Chrome, Firefox, Edge and Safari. Write your scripts in Java, Python, C#, Ruby, JavaScript or Kotlin using the official W3C WebDriver standard . Get started Using AI agents Works out of the box: Selenium downloads what it needs to talk to your browser, so there is nothing to install by hand. Install Selenium and run your first script Add the Selenium package for your language, then run the script below. It opens Chrome, loads a page and closes the browser again. Java Python CSharp Ruby JavaScript Kotlin Add org.seleniumhq.selenium:selenium-java to your build, then run: package dev.selenium.hello ; import org.openqa.selenium.WebDriver ; import org.openqa.selenium.chrome.ChromeDriver ; public class HelloSelenium { public static void main ( String [] args ) { WebDriver driver = new ChromeDriver (); driver . get ( \"https://selenium.dev\" ); driver . quit (); } } View on GitHub Install the package: pip install selenium Then run: from selenium import webdriver driver = webdriver . Chrome () driver . get ( \"http://selenium.dev\" ) driver . quit () View on GitHub Install the package: dotnet add package Selenium.WebDriver Then run: using OpenQA.Selenium.Chrome ; namespace SeleniumDocs.Hello ; public static class HelloSelenium { public static void Main () { var driver = new ChromeDriver (); driver . Navigate (). GoToUrl ( \"https://selenium.dev\" ); driver . Quit (); } } View on GitHub Install the gem: gem install selenium-webdriver Then run: # frozen_string_literal: true require 'selenium-webdriver' driver = Selenium :: WebDriver . for :chrome driver . get 'https://selenium.dev' driver . quit View on GitHub Install the package: npm install selenium-webdriver Then run: const { Builder , Browser } = require ( 'selenium-webdriver' ); ( async function helloSelenium () { let driver = await new Builder (). forBrowser ( Browser . CHROME ). build (); await driver . get ( 'https://selenium.dev' ); await driver . quit (); })(); View on GitHub Kotlin uses the Java bindings. Add org.seleniumhq.selenium:selenium-java to your build, then run: package dev.selenium.hello import org.openqa.selenium.chrome.ChromeDriver fun main () { val driver = ChromeDriver () driver . get ( \"https://selenium.dev\" ) driver . quit () } View on GitHub Need more detail? Follow the Getting Started guide . Pick your tool Selenium WebDriver Use this when you want to drive a browser from code in your own language. WebDriver is a collection of language-specific bindings that control a real browser the way a user would, and it is the foundation for everything else Selenium does. Read more Selenium Grid Use this when you need to run your WebDriver tests on several machines, browsers and operating systems at once. Grid distributes sessions from a central point so you can run against a vast combination of environments in parallel. Read more Used by projects and teams including 32,000+ GitHub stars Moodle Mozilla Progress trivago Does your organisation use Selenium? Add your logo Logos are trademarks of their respective owners. Showing them does not mean these organisations endorse Selenium. The Wikimedia Foundation logo is a trademark of the Wikimedia Foundation and is used with the permission of the Wikimedia Foundation. We are not endorsed by or affiliated with the Wikimedia Foundation. Jenkins logo by the Jenkins project , CC BY-SA 3.0 . Development Partners Selenium Level Sponsors News Selenium 4.52 Released! Thursday, October 29, 2026 By Diego Molina @diemol Today we&rsquo;re happy to announce that Selenium 4.52 has been released! Read More Selenium 4.51 Released! Friday, October 09, 2026 By Diego Molina @diemol Today we&rsquo;re happy to announce that Selenium 4.51 has been released! Read More Selenium 4.50 Released! Wednesday, September 30, 2026 By Diego Molina @diemol Today 