        "evidenceText": "Equality Fund Global Journalism Fellowship 2026–2027 - GFMD « Back to all Fundings Equality Fund Global Journalism Fellowship 2026–2027 Organisation: Equality Fund Status: Open Type: Fellowship Theme: Gender equality in media Funding Size: CAD 4,000 Deadline: 11/11/2026 Eligibility: five journalists located in ODA-recipient countries Target Region: ODA-eligible countries Application Language: English The Equality Fund has launched its inaugural Global Journalism Fellowship, developed in partnership with Canadian Journalists for Free Expression (CJFE) and African Women in Media (AWiM). The fellowship seeks to surface stories of local solutions to global crises, with a particular focus on gender, by selecting up to five journalists located in ODA-recipient countries. Fellows will spend six months in structured programming followed by three additional months to finalise publication (January–September 2027), receiving a CAD 4,000 stipend, up to CAD 500 in reporting expenses, monthly expert-led online sessions, safety training from the International Women’s Media Foundation (IWMF) and the Freedom of the Press Foundation, and an in-person convening with travel costs covered. The programme is particularly interested in stories that move beyond documenting problems and explore locally driven responses to challenges such as climate change, gender-based violence, economic injustice, conflict, or threats to democracy and human rights. Eligibility Open to full-time or independent freelance journalists working on any journalism platform, including text, digital, video, and audio Minimum of three years of journalism experience Journalists must be located in, and be reporting on, communities in ODA-recipient countries (full country list at oecd.org) Must have three strong journalism samples that showcase a range of relevant work Ability to accommodate meetings within daytime hours in Eastern Standard Time Must be fluent in English, Equality Fund’s working 