        "evidenceText": "Morgan Stanley Sustainable Finance Fellowship Program 2027 (Paid) – Opportunity Desk Close Menu Home Conferences Training Scholarships Undergraduate Short Courses Online Courses Masters/Postgraduate PhD Postdoctoral Study Abroad Study in Africa Study in Asia Study in Australia Study in Europe Study in USA Competitions Awards Grants Fellowships Jobs Internships Volunteering Blog OD Specials OD Live Series Young Person of the Month Mentorship OD Mentors Success Stories How-To General Tips ODIC 2025 ODIC 2025 Application ODIC Judges ODIC 2025 Winners ODIC 2023 Winners ODIC 2022 Winners ODIC 2021 Winners ODIC 2019 Winners ODIC 2018 Winners ODIC 2017 Winners ODIC 2016 Winners Search Asia Africa Australia and Oceania America Europe Deadlines Approaching Facebook X (Twitter) Instagram Tuesday, November 10 Facebook X (Twitter) LinkedIn Instagram Telegram Morgan Stanley Sustainable Finance Fellowship Program 2027 (Paid) Jude Ogar October 30, 2026 3 Mins Read Facebook Twitter WhatsApp Pinterest LinkedIn Tumblr Email Telegram Deadline: November 13, 2026 Applications are invited for the Morgan Stanley Sustainable Finance Fellowship Program 2027 . The Sustainable Finance Summer Fellowship provides a unique opportunity to work with Morgan Stanley teams that seek to drive capital toward investments that promote sustainable economic growth and scalable solutions to global challenges. With support from across the Global Sustainability Office (GSO) and the Institute for Sustainable Investing, Morgan Stanley is dedicated to accelerating the adoption of sustainable investing, which seeks to deliver both competitive financial returns and positive environmental and social impact. GSO and the Institute partner across the Firm to pioneer scalable sustainable finance solutions, build new sustainable investing tools and generate industry-leading insights that inform and empower investors. The 10-week Sustainable Finance Summer Fellowship runs from early June to mid-August and places current graduate students on sustainability- or impact-focused teams at Morgan Stanley. Each Fellow will be assigned to a team based on their interests, skills and Firm needs. Past placement teams have included the Global Sustainability Office, Global Capital Markets (GCM), Private Credit & Equity (PC&E) and Wealth Management Investing with Impact (IIP). This program requires in-person attendance for the full 10 weeks in Morgan Stanley’s New York City offices. Responsibilities Fellowship projects will vary depending on which team a Fellow is placed with, but responsibilities may include: Conducting strategic business analysis and detailed industry research Building complex financial models Preparing and delivering presentations in a clear and compelling manner Monitoring and providing updates on market news Researching and analyzing emerging industry trends Gathering and analyzing data Contributing to and/or leading projects that support sustainable investing initiatives Benefits Expected base pay rate for the role will be $135,000 USD per year at the commencement of employment. However, base pay is only part of the total compensation package, which, depending on the position, may also include discretionary bonuses and other Morgan Stanley-sponsored benefit programs. Eligibility Be currently working toward a master’s degree or enrolled in a graduate-level program; Possess a clear and demonstrable interest in sustainability and finance; Be able to summarize and articulate complex ideas effectively; Be a team player and a self-starter who enjoys working on projects independently and in groups; Possess strong organizational skills and the ability to work under tight deadlines; Manage multiple projects and stakeholders efficiently. Application Submit a resume and, separately, answer the following question in no more than 300 words: What is one sustainability issue or theme that you believe deserves greater attention from investors, businesses or policymakers? Why do you think it is often overlooked, and what are the consequences if it continues to receive insufficient attention? Click here to apply For more information, visit Morgan Stanley Sustainable Finance Fellowship . Share. Facebook Twitter WhatsApp LinkedIn Email Pinterest Telegram Previous Article Gates Foundation AI Fellow Program 2027 Next Article Tobin Center/Economics Pre-Doctoral Fellows Program at Yale University 2027-2028 Jude Ogar Website Jude Ogar is an educator and youth development practitioner with years of experience working in the education and youth development space. He is passionate about the development of youth in Africa. Related Posts Wave Winter Research Fellowship 2026-2027 November 10, 2026 Closes in 3 days Career Pathways Initiative Fellowship 2027 November 10, 2026 Closes in 80 days Nature Culture Fellowship 2027 November 10, 2026 Closes in 21 days Search for: Receive Opportunity Alerts! Join over 100,000 email subscribers to receive weekly summary of opportunities. Sign up here . OD YPOM – Sameer Ali Khan Sameer Ali Khan is OD Young Person of the Month – October 2026. Read more . Latest Posts Wave Winter Research Fellowship 2026-2027 Career Pathways Initiative Fellowship 2027 Nature Culture Fellowship 2027 Debt Accountability Journalism Fellowship 2027 for Nigerian Journalists Computation & Cognition Tübingen Summer (CaCTüS) Internship Program 2027 Obama Foundation Leaders Program 2027-2028 Chatham House Research Fellow Africa Programme 2026-2027 QNX Global Hackathon 2026 ($50,000 in prizes) Follow on Twitter Tweets by @OpportunityDesk Follow Us on Social Media Submit Type above and press Enter to search. Press Esc to cancel. Ad Blocker Enabled! Our website is made possible by displaying online advertisements to our visitors. Please support us by disabling your Ad Blocker.",
