        "pageDescription": "",
        "evidenceText": "Fund for Investigative Journalism Seed Grants for Early Reporting – Grants for Journalists Skip to content View Full List Grant details View all grants Fund for Investigative Journalism Seed Grants for Early Reporting Seed funding covers expenses of preliminary reporting, such as open-records requests and initial reporting trips. Journalists do not need a commit to publish. These grants are intended to help yield initial findings that reporter can use to secure a commitment to publish and apply for a full grant from the Fund or other sources. Journalists submit a shorter narrative explaining the investigative story idea and what expenses the grant would cover. Location All Locations (Open to Anyone) Funding Type Fellowship Organization Fund for Investigative Journalism Focus Area Investigative Journalism Subject Area Investigative Journalism Award Size $1,000-$2,500 Career Stage Editor's Note Deadline 01/29/2027 Apply Here",
