        "pageTitle": "Cannes Lions Scholarship 2027 (Fully-funded) &#8211; Opportunity Desk",
        "pageDescription": "",
        "evidenceText": "Cannes Lions Scholarship 2027 (Fully-funded) – Opportunity Desk Close Menu Home Conferences Training Scholarships Undergraduate Short Courses Online Courses Masters/Postgraduate PhD Postdoctoral Study Abroad Study in Africa Study in Asia Study in Australia Study in Europe Study in USA Competitions Awards Grants Fellowships Jobs Internships Volunteering Blog OD Specials OD Live Series Young Person of the Month Mentorship OD Mentors Success Stories How-To General Tips ODIC 2025 ODIC 2025 Application ODIC Judges ODIC 2025 Winners ODIC 2023 Winners ODIC 2022 Winners ODIC 2021 Winners ODIC 2019 Winners ODIC 2018 Winners ODIC 2017 Winners ODIC 2016 Winners Search Asia Africa Australia and Oceania America Europe Deadlines Approaching Facebook X (Twitter) Instagram Tuesday, November 10 Facebook X (Twitter) LinkedIn Instagram Telegram Cannes Lions Scholarship 2027 (Fully-funded) Jude Ogar November 5, 2026 1 Min Read Facebook Twitter WhatsApp Pinterest LinkedIn Tumblr Email Telegram Deadline: December 4, 2026 Applications are open for the Cannes Lions Scholarship 2027 . For Cannes Lions 2027, they are offering 10 fully funded scholarships to underrepresented talent within the creative industry. The LIONS Scholarship is designed to support the next generation of talent, placing an emphasis on diversity of location, gender, race, class, preference and perspective. With five places available in the Brand Marketers Academy and five in the Creative Academy, a total of 10 under-30s from 10 countries will be accepted for the Scholarship. Benefits If you’re selected, you’ll get a fully funded trip to Cannes Lions 2027, including accommodation, travel and allowance. You’ll also get a Young Lions Festival pass, which will give you access to inspiring classroom sessions with world-class speakers, hands-on learning and coaching from industry legends. Eligibility Open to people born on or after 26 June 1997. The minimum age for applying is 18 years old, and proof of age will be required. You’ll also need to have a minimum of two years’ work experience in a role to be eligible. The LIONS Academies are presented in English. Application Click here to apply For more information, visit Cannes Lions Scholarship . Share. Facebook Twitter WhatsApp LinkedIn Email Pinterest Telegram Previous Article Friedrich Ebert Foundation (FES) Young Leaders Program 2027 Next Article ILO Writing Competitions on Safe Labour Migration in East and Horn of Africa 2027 Jude Ogar Website Jude Ogar is an educator and youth development practitioner with years of experience working in the education and youth development space. He is passionate about the development of youth in Africa. Related Posts How to Get a Scholarship with a Third-Class Degree: 7 Practical Steps to Improve Your Chances November 7, 2026 How to Ace Your Scholarship Interview: 12 Tips to Help You Stand Out November 5, 2026 15 Global Scholarship Opportunities Currently Open – November 5, 2026 November 5, 2026 Search for: Receive Opportunity Alerts! Join over 100,000 email subscribers to receive weekly summary of opportunities. Sign up here . OD YPOM – Sameer Ali Khan Sameer Ali Khan is OD Young Person of the Month – October 2026. Read more . Latest Posts Wave Winter Research Fellowship 2026-2027 Career Pathways Initiative Fellowship 2027 Nature Culture Fellowship 2027 Debt Accountability Journalism Fellowship 2027 for Nigerian Journalists Computation & Cognition Tübingen Summer (CaCTüS) Internship Program 2027 Obama Foundation Leaders Program 2027-2028 Chatham House Research Fellow Africa Programme 2026-2027 QNX Global Hackathon 2026 ($50,000 in prizes) Follow on Twitter Tweets by @OpportunityDesk Follow Us on Social Media Submit Type above and press Enter to search. Press Esc to cancel. Ad Blocker Enabled! Our website is made possible by displaying online advertisements to our visitors. Please support us by disabling your Ad Blocker.",
