        "evidenceText": "15 Global Scholarship Opportunities Currently Open – November 5, 2026 – Opportunity Desk Close Menu Home Conferences Training Scholarships Undergraduate Short Courses Online Courses Masters/Postgraduate PhD Postdoctoral Study Abroad Study in Africa Study in Asia Study in Australia Study in Europe Study in USA Competitions Awards Grants Fellowships Jobs Internships Volunteering Blog OD Specials OD Live Series Young Person of the Month Mentorship OD Mentors Success Stories How-To General Tips ODIC 2025 ODIC 2025 Application ODIC Judges ODIC 2025 Winners ODIC 2023 Winners ODIC 2022 Winners ODIC 2021 Winners ODIC 2019 Winners ODIC 2018 Winners ODIC 2017 Winners ODIC 2016 Winners Search Asia Africa Australia and Oceania America Europe Deadlines Approaching Facebook X (Twitter) Instagram Tuesday, November 10 Facebook X (Twitter) LinkedIn Instagram Telegram 15 Global Scholarship Opportunities Currently Open – November 5, 2026 Favour Abatang November 5, 2026 8 Mins Read Facebook Twitter WhatsApp Pinterest LinkedIn Tumblr Email Telegram 1. WAAW Foundation Scholarship 2027 for Female College Students in Africa The WAAW Foundation Scholarship supports female university students of African origin who are studying STEM-related courses at universities or colleges in Africa. The one-time award of US$500 is intended for students who demonstrate financial need, strong academic performance, leadership, volunteering and commitment to giving back to their communities. Eligible applicants are generally first- or second-year undergraduate students, or third-year students enrolled in five-year programmes, and must be below age 32. Scholars are also encouraged to promote women’s participation in STEM through outreach activities at their universities. Click here to apply | Deadline: Unspecified 2. Mastercard Foundation Scholars Program at Sciences Po 2027 (Fully-funded) The Mastercard Foundation Scholars Program at Sciences Po supports talented students from Africa to pursue a two-year master’s degree at Sciences Po in France. The fully funded programme is designed for applicants who demonstrate academic strength, leadership potential and significant financial need, including eligible refugees and students from recognised partner institutions or bridge programmes. Selected scholars receive comprehensive financial support throughout their studies as well as access to academic, professional and leadership-development opportunities. Applicants must meet the programme’s citizenship, age and academic requirements and must not already hold or be pursuing a master’s degree. Click here to apply | Deadline: Dec. 14 3. Mastercard Foundation Scholars Program at ALCHE 2027 (Fully-funded) The Mastercard Foundation Scholars Program at the African Leadership College of Higher Education provides full-ride scholarships to talented young Africans who would otherwise be unable to afford university study. The award covers full tuition and additional financial support throughout the scholar’s journey at ALCHE. Applicants should demonstrate strong academic potential, substantial financial need, leadership ability and a record of contributing to their communities. Female applicants, young people with disabilities and candidates aged 26 and below are especially encouraged to apply, subject to ALCHE admission and study-permit requirements. Click here to apply | Deadline: Unspecified 4. Science, Mathematics, and Research for Transformation (SMART) Scholarship-for-Service Program 2027/2028 The SMART Scholarship-for-Service Program supports students pursuing degrees in science, technology, engineering and mathematics while preparing them for careers within the United States Department of Defense. The programme combines substantial educational funding with mentorship, summer internships and post-graduation employment opportunities. Eligible applicants may be pursuing undergraduate or graduate study in approved STEM disciplines and must satisfy the programme’s citizenship, academic and security requirements. The scholarship is particularly suited to students seeking a funded education pathway linked directly to professional experience and public-service employment. Click here to apply | Deadline: Dec. 4 5. AHRC Doctoral Landscape Scholarship Awards at Birmingham City University 2027 The AHRC Doctoral Landscape Awards at Birmingham City University provide funded doctoral opportunities for researchers working in arts and humanities disciplines. The awards are designed to support high-quality PhD research while giving scholars access to research training, supervisory expertise and wider professional-development opportunities. Applicants should present a strong research proposal aligned with the university’s eligible subject areas and demonstrate the academic preparation required for doctoral study. Candidates should also carefully review the university’s application and nomination requirements before submission. Click here to apply | Deadline: Nov. 16 6. Swedish Institute Pioneering Women in STEM Scholarship 2027 (Fully-funded) The Swedish Institute Pioneering Women in STEM Scholarship supports women from eligible countries in Africa and Asia to pursue full-time master’s studies in Sweden. The fully funded award covers tuition fees, provides a monthly living allowance of SEK 12,000 and includes a one-time travel grant, alongside access to the SI Network for Global Professionals and the Sweden Alumni Network. Applicants must apply for an eligible STEM master’s programme and demonstrate relevant work and leadership experience. The scholarship is designed for women committed to using science, technology, engineering and mathematics to drive innovation and sustainable change. Click here to apply | Deadline: Jan. 15 7. Swedish Institute (SI) Scholarship for Global Professionals 2027 (Fully-funded) The SI Scholarship for Global Professionals offers fully funded master’s study in Sweden for professionals from eligible countries who have demonstrated work experience and leadership potential. The award covers full tuition fees, provides a monthly allowance of SEK 12,000, includes a travel grant and gives scholars access to professional and alumni networks. Eligible fields include governance, public health, entrepreneurship and innovation, and STEM. Applicants must first apply for an eligible Swedish master’s programme and meet the scholarship’s citizenship, tuition-liability, work-experience and leadership requirements. Click here to apply | Deadline: Jan. 15 8. Toronto Metropolitan University Global Migration Institute Scholarships 2027-2028 The Toronto Metropolitan University Global Migration Institute Scholarships support full-time master’s and PhD students whose research relates to migration and one of the Bridging Divides programme’s core themes. Funding can provide up to CAD $35,000 per year for eligible master’s students and up to CAD $45,000 per year for eligible PhD students, subject to programme conditions and annual review. Recipients are integrated into the Global Migration Institute’s research community and participate in training, workshops and professional-development activities. Applicants must be studying or applying to study at Toronto Metropolitan University and have appropriate supervision connected to the programme. Click here to apply | Deadline: Apr. 1 9. France Excellence Eiffel Scholarship Program 2026-2027 The France Excellence Eiffel Scholarship Program supports outstanding international students pursuing master’s and doctoral programmes in France. Developed by the French Ministry for Europe and Foreign Affairs, the programme focuses on priority fields including biology and health, ecological transition, mathematics and digital technologies, engineering, law and political science, economics and management, and French language and civilisation. Master’s scholars receive a monthly allowance and additional services such as travel, insurance and housing support, while doctoral scholars receive a higher monthly stipend and similar benefits. Candidates must be nominated by a French higher education institution, as direct applications from students are not accepted. Click here to apply | Deadline: Unspecified 10. Yenching Academy at Peking University 2027 – Full Scholarship for Master’s Study in China The Yenching Academy at Peking University offers a fully funded interdisciplinary master’s programme for outstanding students interested in understanding China and its role in the world. The scholarship supports tuition, accommodation, a monthly stipend, one round-trip travel allowance and field-study costs. Applicants should have a strong academic record, leadership potential and evidence of engagement beyond the classroom, and must hold or be completing a bachelor’s degree before enrolment. The programme brings together an international cohort and allows students to pursue research across a wide range of China-related academic fields. Click here to apply | Deadline: Nov. 30 11. Asian Development Bank-Japan Scholarship Program 2026 The Asian Development Bank-Japan Scholarship Program supports eligible citizens of ADB developing member countries to pursue postgraduate study in development-related fields. The Opportunity Desk listing highlights master’s study at the University of Hawai‘i at Mānoa alongside educational and leadership activities at the East-West Center. Support may include tuition and fees, round-trip travel, housing, a monthly stipend, textbooks, health insurance and visa sponsorship. Applicants generally need a qualifying bachelor’s degree, relevant professional experience, strong English proficiency and a commitment to return home and contribute to development after their studies. Click here to apply | Deadline: Dec. 1 12. Hong Kong PhD Fellowship Scheme (HKPFS) 2027/2028 The Hong Kong PhD Fellowship Scheme attracts outstanding students from around the world to undertake full-time doctoral study at eight participating universities in Hong Kong. Selection considers academic excellence, research ability and potential, communication and interpersonal skills, and leadership. The fellowship provides an annual stipend of HK$344,400 and a conference and research-related travel allowance of HK$14,400 per year for up to three years, with additional support potentially available from universities where more time is required. Applicants first submit an initial HKPFS application and then apply for PhD admission to their selected participating institution or institutions. Click here to apply | Deadline: Dec. 1 13. Overseas Press Club Foundation Scholar Awards 2027 The Overseas Press Club Foundation Scholar Awards support undergraduate and graduate students who want to build careers in international journalism. Eligible applicants include students enrolled at North American colleges and universities as well as American students studying abroad who have demonstrated a clear interest in international reporting. Winners receive either a US$3,000 scholarship for independent work or a US$4,000 fellowship supporting experience at a leading news bureau. Applications require a cover letter, résumé and an appropriate journalism work sample that demonstrates the applicant’s interests, skills and international focus. Click here to apply | Deadline: Nov. 15 14. Girls On Campus She Leads Scholarship 2026 (up to $1,500) The Girls On Campus She Leads Scholarship supports incoming and current undergraduate students studying at accredited colleges or universities in the United States. The US$1,500 award recognises academic effort, financial need, community impact, leadership potential and commitment to gender equity and personal growth. Applicants of any citizenship or immigration status may apply, including international students, DACA recipients and undocumented students, provided they meet the education requirements. Candidates submit an essay addressing barriers faced by women of colour in higher education and how they plan to respond to those challenges. Click here to apply | Deadline: Nov. 25 15. Johns Hopkins SAIS Public Service Scholars – Scholarship Program 2026 The Johns Hopkins SAIS Public Service Scholars programme supports experienced professionals pursuing the Master of International Public Policy in Washington, DC who have a strong public-service background and plan to return to public service after graduation. Scholars can receive up to a 50 percent tuition scholarship alongside curated lectures, seminars, career guidance and opportunities to engage with public-sector leaders and alumni. Applicants of all nationalities may be considered and should demonstrate leadership, academic aptitude and sustained commitment to public service, with additional consideration given to financial need. Candidates must apply for fall admission to the MIPP programme and complete the required institutional-aid and scholarship materials. Click here to apply | Deadline: Unspecified For more scholarships, visit OD Scholarships. Share. Facebook Twitter WhatsApp LinkedIn Email Pinterest Telegram Previous Article IX-WAI Early Career Development Grant 2027 (up to £1,000) Next Article Young Security Conference (YSC) Fellowship 2026 Favour Abatang Facebook X (Twitter) Instagram LinkedIn Favour Abatang is a Non-profit Executive and International Development Expert with experience leading an organisation, curating programs, and fundraising. She has made significant strides in supporting teenage mothers and at-risk girls through tailored second-chance opportunities. She is currently expanding her impact as the Community Manager at Opportunity Desk. Related Posts 21 Hot Job Opportunities Currently Open – November 7, 2026 November 7, 2026 How to Turn Your Passion into Income: 5 Practical Ways to Make Money Doing What You Love November 7, 2026 How to Get a Scholarship with a Third-Class Degree: 7 Practical Steps to Improve Your Chances November 7, 2026 Search for: Receive Opportunity Alerts! Join over 100,000 email subscribers to receive weekly summary of opportunities. Sign up here . OD YPOM – Sameer Ali Khan Sameer Ali Khan is OD Young Person of the Month – October 2026. Read more . Latest Posts Wave Winter Research Fellowship 2026-2027 Career Pathways Initiative Fellowship 2027 Nature Culture Fellowship 2027 Debt Accountability Journalism Fellowship 2027 for Nigerian Journalists Computation & Cognition Tübingen Summer (CaCTüS) Internship Program 2027 Obama Foundation Leaders Program 2027-2028 Chatham House Research Fellow Africa Programme 2026-2027 QNX Global Hackathon 2026 ($50,000 in prizes) Follow on Twitter Tweets by @OpportunityDesk Follow Us on Social Media Submit Type above and press Enter to search. Press Esc to cancel. Ad Blocker Enabled! Our website is made possible by displaying online advertisements to our visitors. Please support us by disabling your Ad Blocker.",
