        "evidenceText": "Call for judges : Join the OD Impact Challenge 2026 global judging panel – Opportunity Desk Close Menu Home Conferences Training Scholarships Undergraduate Short Courses Online Courses Masters/Postgraduate PhD Postdoctoral Study Abroad Study in Africa Study in Asia Study in Australia Study in Europe Study in USA Competitions Awards Grants Fellowships Jobs Internships Volunteering Blog OD Specials OD Live Series Young Person of the Month Mentorship OD Mentors Success Stories How-To General Tips ODIC 2025 ODIC 2025 Application ODIC Judges ODIC 2025 Winners ODIC 2023 Winners ODIC 2022 Winners ODIC 2021 Winners ODIC 2019 Winners ODIC 2018 Winners ODIC 2017 Winners ODIC 2016 Winners Search Asia Africa Australia and Oceania America Europe Deadlines Approaching Facebook X (Twitter) Instagram Tuesday, November 10 Facebook X (Twitter) LinkedIn Instagram Telegram Call for judges : Join the OD Impact Challenge 2026 global judging panel Favour Abatang November 7, 2026 2 Mins Read Facebook Twitter WhatsApp Pinterest LinkedIn Tumblr Email Telegram Are you passionate about youth leadership, innovation and social impact? Opportunity Desk invites experienced professionals, entrepreneurs, development practitioners and industry leaders to join the global judging panel for the  Opportunity Desk Impact Challenge (ODIC) 2026 . The OD Impact Challenge is an annual global competition that recognises and supports young changemakers aged 18–30 who are creating positive change in their communities. Through the challenge, young people showcase their initiatives, share their impact stories and gain access to opportunities that strengthen their work. As a judge, you will play an important role in identifying outstanding young changemakers and recognising innovative solutions addressing social, economic and environmental challenges. Why become a judge? Make an impact:  Help recognise and support promising youth-led initiatives. Share your expertise:  Contribute your knowledge to evaluating innovative projects. Connect globally:  Engage with professionals and changemakers from diverse backgrounds. Support young leaders:  Help identify initiatives with the potential to create lasting change. Who can apply? We welcome applications from professionals with experience in social impact, entrepreneurship, innovation, sustainability, international development, project management, monitoring and evaluation, education, gender equality and related fields. Applicants should demonstrate sound judgement, integrity and a commitment to supporting young changemakers. Previous judging or project evaluation experience is an advantage. Responsibilities Selected judges will review applications, assess project innovation, community impact and sustainability, and contribute to a fair and transparent selection process. How to apply Interested applicants should complete the online application form, providing details of their professional experience, expertise and motivation for joining the judging panel. Deadline: November 30, 2026 – Click here to apply Lend Your Expertise. Discover Changemakers. Shape Global Impact. Share. Facebook Twitter WhatsApp LinkedIn Email Pinterest Telegram Previous Article Global Changemakers’ Media Impact Academy 2027 for Youth in the USA (A chance to win a $1,000 grant) Next Article Arewa Creative Writing and Advocacy Fellowship (ACWAF) 2026 – Cohort 1 Favour Abatang Facebook X (Twitter) Instagram LinkedIn Favour Abatang is a Non-profit Executive and International Development Expert with experience leading an organisation, curating programs, and fundraising. She has made significant strides in supporting teenage mothers and at-risk girls through tailored second-chance opportunities. She is currently expanding her impact as the Community Manager at Opportunity Desk. Related Posts 21 Hot Job Opportunities Currently Open – November 7, 2026 November 7, 2026 How to Turn Your Passion into Income: 5 Practical Ways to Make Money Doing What You Love November 7, 2026 Growing Your Business with Venture Funding: 5 Practical Steps for Entrepreneurs November 5, 2026 Search for: Receive Opportunity Alerts! Join over 100,000 email subscribers to receive weekly summary of opportunities. Sign up here . OD YPOM – Sameer Ali Khan Sameer Ali Khan is OD Young Person of the Month – October 2026. Read more . Latest Posts Wave Winter Research Fellowship 2026-2027 Career Pathways Initiative Fellowship 2027 Nature Culture Fellowship 2027 Debt Accountability Journalism Fellowship 2027 for Nigerian Journalists Computation & Cognition Tübingen Summer (CaCTüS) Internship Program 2027 Obama Foundation Leaders Program 2027-2028 Chatham House Research Fellow Africa Programme 2026-2027 QNX Global Hackathon 2026 ($50,000 in prizes) Follow on Twitter Tweets by @OpportunityDesk Follow Us on Social Media Submit Type above and press Enter to search. Press Esc to cancel. Ad Blocker Enabled! Our website is made possible by displaying online advertisements to our visitors. Please support us by disabling your Ad Blocker.",
