      "verificationStatus": null,
      "audit": {
        "checkedAt": "2026-11-10T20:36:10.810Z",
        "httpStatus": 200,
        "finalUrl": "https://opportunitydesk.org/2026/11/07/cega-visiting-fellowship-2027-2028/",
        "contentType": "text/html; charset=UTF-8",
        "pageTitle": "Center for Effective Global Action (CEGA) Visiting Fellowship 2027-2028 &#8211; Opportunity Desk",
        "pageDescription": "",
        "evidenceText": "Center for Effective Global Action (CEGA) Visiting Fellowship 2027-2028 – Opportunity Desk Close Menu Home Conferences Training Scholarships Undergraduate Short Courses Online Courses Masters/Postgraduate PhD Postdoctoral Study Abroad Study in Africa Study in Asia Study in Australia Study in Europe Study in USA Competitions Awards Grants Fellowships Jobs Internships Volunteering Blog OD Specials OD Live Series Young Person of the Month Mentorship OD Mentors Success Stories How-To General Tips ODIC 2025 ODIC 2025 Application ODIC Judges ODIC 2025 Winners ODIC 2023 Winners ODIC 2022 Winners ODIC 2021 Winners ODIC 2019 Winners ODIC 2018 Winners ODIC 2017 Winners ODIC 2016 Winners Search Asia Africa Australia and Oceania America Europe Deadlines Approaching Facebook X (Twitter) Instagram Tuesday, November 10 Facebook X (Twitter) LinkedIn Instagram Telegram Center for Effective Global Action (CEGA) Visiting Fellowship 2027-2028 Jude Ogar November 7, 2026 3 Mins Read Facebook Twitter WhatsApp Pinterest LinkedIn Tumblr Email Telegram Deadline: January 17, 2027 Applications are open for the Center for Effective Global Action (CEGA) Visiting Fellowship 2027-2028 . The Center for Effective Global Action (CEGA) invites African researchers and practitioners interested in developing their skills in impact evaluation to apply for its Fellowship Program to be completed in Fall 2027 or Spring 2028. Selected fellows will audit coursework, develop skills in quantitative development research, access a personalized mentorship program to develop their research ideas, and build their research networks. Fellows will spend 16 weeks either in residence at UC Berkeley or participating virtually. Applicants can apply to one of two tracks–the Practitioner Track or the Academic Track–as either a Resident (in-person at UC Berkeley) or Non-Resident (online) Fellow. Fellows will be given the choice of either Fall 2027 (August through December) or Spring 2028 (January through May). Eligibility Across both tracks: To be accepted to the CEGA Fellowship, applicants must demonstrate the following: Be fluent in English (written and spoken), and a strong communicator. Be from an East African or West African country and have completed at least up to secondary school education in an African institution. Have at least a Master’s degree, are currently enrolled in a PhD, or have completed a PhD (within 8 years) in economics, political science, statistics, epidemiology/public health, or another social science discipline. Plan to return to an institution in East or West Africa after the fellowship. If currently enrolled in a PhD program outside the African continent, scholars may complete their PhD before their return. The Practitioner Track is intended for professionals interested in improving their research skills to grow in their careers in African government ministries, think tanks, or NGOs. Applicants to the Practitioner Track should: Work for an NGO, think tank, or government ministry in East or West Africa, with a goal to grow into more senior careers. Be actively using or promoting the use of evidence to improve economic and social well-being for populations. The Academic Track is intended for early career scholars who intend to pursue an academic career. Application to the Academic Track should: Either be a doctoral student or hold a current staff position within a university or research institution, preferably one that supports policy-relevant, quantitative social science research. Be prepared to develop their own research proposal and/or be embedded within a faculty’s existing research project. Resident fellows must be from a country eligible for a J-1 visa under current U.S. visa requirements: Djibouti, Ethiopia, Ghana, Guinea, Guinea-Bissau, Kenya, Liberia, Madagascar, Mauritius, Mozambique, Rwanda, Seychelles, Uganda. Note that this is subject to change dependent on US regulations. Non-Resident fellows will be prioritized from currently subject to U.S. visa restrictions: Benin, Burkina Faso, Burundi, Cote d’Ivoire, The Gambia, Malawi, Mali, Mauritania, Niger, Nigeria, Senegal, Sierra Leone, Tanzania, Togo, Zambia, and Zimbabwe Application The application deadline is 5:00 PM GMT on January 17, 2027. Click here to apply For more information, visit CEGA Visiting Fellowship . Share. Facebook Twitter WhatsApp LinkedIn Email Pinterest Telegram Previous Article 21 Hot Job Opportunities Currently Open – November 7, 2026 Next Article MCW Global Young Leaders Fellowship 2027 (Funded) Jude Ogar Website Jude Ogar is an educator and youth development practitioner with years of experience working in the education and youth development space. He is passionate about the development of youth in Africa. Related Posts Wave Winter Research Fellowship 2026-2027 November 10, 2026 Closes in 3 days Career Pathways Initiative Fellowship 2027 November 10, 2026 Closes in 80 days Nature Culture Fellowship 2027 November 10, 2026 Closes in 21 days Search for: Receive Opportunity Alerts! Join over 100,000 email subscribers to receive weekly summary of opportunities. Sign up here . OD YPOM – Sameer Ali Khan Sameer Ali Khan is OD Young Person of the Month – October 2026. Read more . Latest Posts Wave Winter Research Fellowship 2026-2027 Career Pathways Initiative Fellowship 2027 Nature Culture Fellowship 2027 Debt Accountability Journalism Fellowship 2027 for Nigerian Journalists Computation & Cognition Tübingen Summer (CaCTüS) Internship Program 2027 Obama Foundation Leaders Program 2027-2028 Chatham House Research Fellow Africa Programme 2026-2027 QNX Global Hackathon 2026 ($50,000 in prizes) Follow on Twitter Tweets by @OpportunityDesk Follow Us on Social Media Submit Type above and press Enter to search. Press Esc to cancel. Ad Blocker Enabled! Our website is made possible by displaying online advertisements to our visitors. Please support us by disabling your Ad Blocker.",
