        "contentType": "text/html; charset=UTF-8",
        "pageTitle": "Poynter ACES Certificates in Editing - Poynter",
        "pageDescription": "The Poynter ACES Certificates in Editing are the journalism and publishing industry standards in editing tutorials for professional editors.",
        "evidenceText": "Poynter ACES Certificates in Editing - Poynter Poynter ACES Certificates in Editing - Poynter DONATE What do you want to search? Submit Sign In | Membership News Training Ethics Fact-Checking Media Literacy AI Events Future of Public Media Newmark Ethics Center IFCN MediaWise PolitiFact Donate About Us Press Freedom Watch The Poynter 50 Podcasts Artificial Intelligence Business & Work Reporting & Editing Fact-Checking Ethics & Trust Local News Journalism, Media & Communication Training Poynter Membership Categories Consulting & Coaching For ACES Members For Local News Funders All Categories Broadcast & Visual Journalism Business & Work Ethics Fact-Checking & Media Literacy Leadership Reporting & Editing Writing Poynter ACES Introductory Certificate in Editing Poynter ACES Intermediate Certificate in Editing Poynter ACES Advanced Certificate in Editing Workshops and Coaching Tools for Funders Ethics Ethics Training Ethics Articles AI Ethics Public Editor Project Get Ethics Advice Fact-Checking Articles IFCN IFCN Grants International Fact-Checking Day Teen Creator Network PolitiFact MediaWise Media Literacy Resources AI Literacy Ambassadors Teen Creator Network Research & News International en Español MediaWise Training All Events The 2026 Poynter Journalism Prizes The Poynter ACES Certificates in Editing serve as the communication industry’s leading training program to help communicators amp up their editing skills, improve their work lives and advance their careers. Regularly updated to reflect evolving industry practices, these courses represent the latest in editing standards, tools and best practices. Communicators at any stage of their professional development can benefit from one or all of our three editing certificate programs: Introductory, Intermediate and Advanced. There are no prerequisites for any of the certificates — learners can choose any or all of the learning paths to level up their editing skills. Each certificate level is made up of a series of six to seven courses and a final assessment. You can enroll in the courses individually; however, you’ll receive a certificate only if you enroll in the certificate program and successfully complete the course assessments offered through it. In addition to our certificate pathways, we offer specialized courses such as Editing Faster with Word Macros, which helps editors save time and improve consistency by automating repetitive tasks. Click below to read more about each certificate, including the list of courses within each, the cost, the estimated time to completion, and to read about the discount applied to the certificates for members of ACES. Still have questions? Please visit our FAQ center here or email info@poynter.org . Poynter ACES Introductory Certificate Gain a solid understanding of standards, skills and best practices when you earn your Poynter ACES Introductory Certificate in Editing. Learn more and enroll Poynter ACES Intermediate Certificate Go deeper into grammar, working with writers, ethics, law and tech with the Poynter ACES Intermediate Certificate in Editing. Learn more and enroll Poynter ACES Advanced Certificate Cultivate skills to become a trusted and credible editor through an improved knowledge of AI, inclusivity, style guide development and freelancing in the Poynter ACES Advanced Certificate in Editing. Learn more and enroll Editing Faster with Word Macros Stop wasting hours on repetitive tasks — automate them instead. Learn to create custom Word shortcuts in Windows or macOS that reduce editing time without sacrificing accuracy and consistency. Learn more and enroll FAQs Have questions about any of our certificates? Check out this FAQ to see if we can provide you with answers. Get help",
