d the country Tom Jones As Democrats swept the midterms, news anchors struggled to find the words Tom Jones Today is the big day … for the pollsters Tom Jones Haley Stevens’ stunning endorsement set off a media firestorm. Will Michigan voters care? Tom Jones There are two Dan Sullivans running for Senate in Alaska. The New York Times found out why Tom Jones The midterms haven’t happened yet, but the election conspiracy theories are already here Tom Jones Buried in Trump’s 1,300-word Bill Maher rant was some news about the press Tom Jones With one week until the midterms, PolitiFact is on the lookout for ‘mischief’ Tom Jones Trump sued the BBC. Now he has to answer its questions. Ren LaForme Brendan Carr warns broadcasters about ‘fake polls’ as a real polling scandal unfolds Amaris Castillo CNN threatens to take the White House back to court over Air Force One access Angela Fu The White House has a workaround when networks refuse to replace CNN Angela Fu President Trump’s losing streak versus the press continues Tom Jones Katie Zacharia’s debut as press secretary went about as badly as it could have Tom Jones The Pentagon plans to livestream an execution. Some Republicans are having second thoughts. Tom Jones Jennifer Griffin has covered 8 defense secretaries. She’s never seen a Pentagon like this. Tom Jones CBS gives JD Vance a prime-time town hall just before the midterms Tom Jones Paramount and Warner Bros. Discovery are finally one company. So what happens now? Tom Jones CNN gets a best-case scenario under its new owners Tom Jones Trump lashes out at Kaitlan Collins, then wakes up angry at Fox News Tom Jones Trump attacks Fox News as Hegseth blasts the press Tom Jones Sen. Eric Schmitt confused the Hawks and Hawkeyes and the political press had a field day Tom Jones Evan Gershkovich spent 491 days imprisoned in Russia. Now he’s telling his story. Tom Jones Rachel Maddow on why Trump keeps attacking the media: ‘You play the hits’ Tom Jones Trump banned three news outlets. A judge let them back in. Then things got weirder. Tom Jones Trump was back on TV, but the network standoff isn’t over Tom Jones ‘This is unprecedented’: Trump’s media bans upend White House coverage Tom Jones What’s behind Trump’s White House media ban — and what happens next Tom Jones The New York Times turns 175 and looks back at the good and the bad Tom Jones ‘Our hearts are broken’: L.A. news stations mourn journalist, pilot killed in helicopter crash Tom Jones Trump’s latest Kennedy Center fight sounds almost made up Tom Jones After months of drama, it was ‘60 Minutes’ of more of the same Tom Jones ESPN gave Ted Cruz 10 minutes on ‘College GameDay.’ Critics say it crossed a line. Tom Jones The stories of 9/11, 25 years later Tom Jones Jeff Bezos likes what he’s seen from The Washington Post’s interim boss Tom Jones What can we expect from the season premiere of ‘60 Minutes?’ Tom Jones The Athletic investigated Dianna Russini’s work. What it found — and what it didn’t find. Ren LaForme Where’s Pete Hegseth? Not on Fox News. Tom Jones Who will hold the next White House press briefing? Tom Jones Trump’s threats against the press don’t have to succeed to do damage Tom Jones Trump calls on the FCC to punish Kristen Welker — for accurate commentary Tom Jones Meta’s $18 billion settlement could reshape social media for young people Tom Jones In a divided country during troubling times, Dolly Parton was the joy we could all agree on Tom Jones Karen Attiah spent a year fighting her Washington Post firing. She just won. Tom Jones How close is FCC chair Brendan Carr to the Trump White House? New records offer a look. Tom Jones A fake poll made real news. What does that say about political polling? Ren LaForme More than 200 AI-generated ‘local news’ sites just went dark Alex Mahadevan An FT column was condensed with AI. It crossed a novel ethical line. Ren LaForme A Washington Post investigation prompts changes at surveillance company Flock Angela Fu Karoline Leavitt to step down as White House press secretary Ren LaForme Trump left Air Force One because of a threat. Journalists stayed aboard. Tom Jones Trump’s FCC is poised for a further shift to the right Tom Jones Q&A: Peter Alexander wants facts, not shouting matches, at MS NOW Tom Jones Trump’s revived Wall Street Journal lawsuit meets more skepticism in court Tom Jones David Ellison broke months of silence on CNN’s future. His biggest critics won’t be reassured. Tom Jones The Trump administration’s hunt for leakers targets yet another journalist Tom Jones Dana Bash did her job — and RFK Jr. didn’t handle it well Tom Jones ABC is done playing defense against the FCC Tom Jones ‘60 Minutes’ makes big hires, including one that will raise eyebrows Tom Jones Savannah Guthrie makes an emotional plea for her missing mother Tom Jones The White House Correspondents’ Association dinner was an embarrassment Tom Jones Left with no options, the Trump administration drops subpoenas against New York Times journalists Tom Jones Is the White House Correspondents’ dinner headed for another mess? Tom Jones ESPN’s latest layoffs claim some of its best-known on-air personalities Tom Jones The Trump administration’s latest media target? A reporter’s mother. Tom Jones Have you gotten health advice from TikTok or Instagram? This is for you. Tom Jones When does a president deserve prime-time television? Tom Jones Should networks air Trump’s national address live? Tom Jones The Paramount-Warner Bros. deal’s new hurdle comes with an asterisk Tom Jones How Air Force One became a press freedom story Tom Jones What’s going to happen to CNN? Tom Jones The Washington Post joins Trump’s growing list of media lawsuit losses Tom Jones ABC reminds the FCC it already ruled ‘The View’ is news Tom Jones Is the FCC’s investigation having a chilling effect on ‘The View’? Tom Jones How reporters uncovered Trump’s role in FIFA’s stunning World Cup reversal Tom Jones CNN’s uncertain future claims its first major