        "pageDescription": "Expert research support for journalists and creators. Verify facts, find hard-to-access records and publish with confidence — without adding staff.",
        "evidenceText": "Poynter Research - Poynter Poynter Research - Poynter DONATE What do you want to search? Submit Sign In | Membership News Training Ethics Fact-Checking Media Literacy AI Events Future of Public Media Newmark Ethics Center IFCN MediaWise PolitiFact Donate About Us Press Freedom Watch The Poynter 50 Podcasts Artificial Intelligence Business & Work Reporting & Editing Fact-Checking Ethics & Trust Local News Journalism, Media & Communication Training Poynter Membership Categories Consulting & Coaching For ACES Members For Local News Funders All Categories Broadcast & Visual Journalism Business & Work Ethics Fact-Checking & Media Literacy Leadership Reporting & Editing Writing Poynter ACES Introductory Certificate in Editing Poynter ACES Intermediate Certificate in Editing Poynter ACES Advanced Certificate in Editing Workshops and Coaching Tools for Funders Ethics Ethics Training Ethics Articles AI Ethics Public Editor Project Get Ethics Advice Fact-Checking Articles IFCN IFCN Grants International Fact-Checking Day Teen Creator Network PolitiFact MediaWise Media Literacy Resources AI Literacy Ambassadors Teen Creator Network Research & News International en Español MediaWise Training All Events The 2026 Poynter Journalism Prizes Poynter Research helps newsrooms, independent journalists, podcasters and influencers uncover hard-to-find facts, verify complex claims and publish with confidence. What this means for your work: Publish with greater trust in your facts, sourcing and framing. Reduce the risk of errors, corrections and legal exposure. Get deep, credible research support without adding staff. Meet tight deadlines without sacrificing quality. Strengthen investigative, longform and enterprise reporting. Journalists and content creators with limited budgets can benefit from our expert research staff and paid tools. Reach out to learn more about how we can support you. How we can help you We tackle your research needs with a staff that has decades of experience in news research and fact-checking, including contributing to Pulitzer Prize winning projects and routinely meeting tight deadlines. We expertly navigate databases, archives and court systems to uncover all available evidence and details that others may overlook. Poynter Research can help you: Verify backgrounds of individuals and businesses, for reporters working on investigative stories, newsrooms inquiring about prospective hires or other cases. Find and retrieve federal and state court documents , including lawsuits, marriage and dissolution of marriage records, criminal records, civil procedures and judgments. Identify expert sources on various topics and reviewing their record for potential conflicts of interest. Line-by-line fact-check of magazine stories, longform journalism, nonfiction books and other written work. Verify videos and images for signs of deceptive editing and artificial intelligence manipulation. Review corporate, marketing and advertising materials for accuracy, grammar and style to ensure a polished finished product. Vet AI-generated content to flag factual errors and eliminate nonsensical information. Trace the origin of conspiracy theories and misinformation narratives. Debunk online scams promoting health products, debt relief and more. Our expert team can empower you to tell stories that leave a long-lasting impression and make a difference. “Our team is really good at getting to the bottom of things. That might mean tracking down records no one else can find, connecting dots that aren’t obvious or just making sure you’re working from information you can actually trust. At the end of the day, we want you to feel confident in what you’re putting out into the world.” Caryn Baird, Poynter staff researcher. Independent, Ethical Research You Can Trust Poynter Research operates under strict ethical and transparency standards designed to protect journalistic independence and client confidentiality. Privacy: Client details and requests remain confidential. Nonpartisanship: We do not work for political candidates, parties or anonymous clients. Clear communication: We promise an ongoing alignment on scope, priorities and deadlines. Fill out our form or email us at research@poynter.org to see how we can help. Get Expert Research Behind Your Story \" * \" indicates required fields Name * First Last Email * Phone * Organization name * Title * What kind of research support are you looking for? * CAPTCHA Δ Team Members Caryn Baird Researcher, Poynter and PolitiFact Caryn Baird is a researcher for PolitiFact and The Poynter Institute. She previously was the senior news researcher at the Tampa Bay Times where for... Read More Sara Swann Digital Research Program Manager, PolitiFact Sara Swann is PolitiFact's digital research program manager. Previously, she was the interim research editor, a digital research analyst and a staff writer for PolitiFact.... Read More Miriam Valverde Assistant Managing Editor, PolitiFact Miriam Valverde is an assistant managing editor at PolitiFact. She oversees Poynter and PolitiFact’s research and custom fact-checking projects, as well as PolitiFact en Español.... Read More",
