om an onboarding specialist—available with a Standard or Premium plan. Learn more To watch this video, you need to accept Performance and Functionality Cookies . For more info, check our cookie policy . We're sorry. Due to a technical issue, the video is currently unable to load. Please try again later. Onboarding services video We offer expert 24/7 customer service Our customer service team is always available and ready to support you if you ever need help. See our support offerings FAQs What is email marketing software? Email marketing software is a tool that helps businesses send emails to customers and prospects at scale. Instead of manually typing out individual messages, you can create, design, and send professional campaigns to hundreds or thousands of people at once. These platforms typically include templates, automation features, analytics, and tools to help you organize your contacts. Whether you're announcing a sale, sharing company news, or nurturing leads, email marketing software streamlines the entire process. What does an email marketing platform do? An email marketing platform handles everything from designing your emails to tracking how well they perform. You can build campaigns using drag-and-drop editors, personalize messages for different audience segments, and schedule sends for optimal timing. Most SMS and email marketing platforms also let you automate repetitive tasks like welcome emails or birthday messages. Beyond sending, the best email marketing platforms provide insights into open rates, click-throughs, and conversions so you can see what's working and what needs adjustment. Basically, it takes the heavy lifting out of staying connected with your audience. How effective is email marketing? Many people ask the question, \" Is email marketing dead? \" The simple answer is that it's very much alive and well. Email marketing is one of the most effective digital marketing channels available. It delivers a strong return on investment because you're reaching people who have already shown an interest in your brand by signing up. With email marketing solutions like Mailchimp, you can target specific groups with personalized content, which drives higher engagement. The benefits of email marketing are direct communication, measurability, and the ability to scale your efforts without proportionally increasing costs. What are the four types of email marketing campaigns? There are many types of email marketing campaigns. However, there are four principal types of marketing emails, which include: Promotional emails: Promotional emails advertise a company’s products or services, often by promoting sales, discounts, seasonal events, company events, and so on. Product update emails: These emails inform customers about new or updated products. Digital newsletters: Digital newsletters are regularly sent to a company’s email list to inform customers of company or industry updates by providing interesting articles or relevant news. Transactional emails: These emails are typically triggered by a customer action. For example, if a customer buys a product, they may receive a confirmation email or a follow-up email that asks for their feedback. How can I optimize email marketing campaigns? Optimizing your campaigns comes down to testing what works and refining based on results. Your subject lines determine whether someone opens your message, so keep them short, relevant, and intriguing without being clickbait-y. Segment your audience so you're sending the right content to the right people — a one-size-fits-all approach rarely works well. Test different send times, layouts, and calls to action to see what resonates. Make sure your emails look good on mobile devices since most people read on their phones. Also, clean your list regularly by removing inactive subscribers to maintain strong deliverability. If you need inspiration, check out these email campaign examples to spark ideas. What makes Mailchimp the best email marketing platform for small, new e-commerce websites? Mailchimp is the best email marketing platform because it's built to help small and medium-sized businesses grow without needing a huge team or technical expertise. You get access to over 130 pre-built email templates designed for e-commerce and retail, so you don't need coding skills to create professional campaigns. Features like dynamic content let you personalize messages automatically, while powerful customer segmentation ensures you're targeting the right shoppers with relevant offers. Abandoned cart emails help recover lost sales by reminding customers about items they've left behind. Mailchimp's user-friendly design tools mean you can start selling and engaging customers right away, even if you're just learning email marketing basics . Is Mailchimp's email marketing platform reliable? Can it handle high-volume sends? Absolutely. Mailchimp's infrastructure powers millions of emails every day for over 11 million customers globally. The platform maintains an average delivery rate for transactional and marketing emails above 99%, which means your messages actually reach inboxes instead of getting lost or marked as spam. Mailchimp customers have sent more than 3.1 billion emails using AI-generated content, proving our system can handle serious volume. Whether you're sending emails to a few hundred subscribers or scaling up to hundreds of thousands, you can count on fast, secure delivery with proven deliverability rates. What makes Mailchimp the best email marketing service for sending sales emails? Sales teams need ways to stay connected with prospects and clients. Mailchimp lets you send professional, branded emails that look polished and build trust with recipients. You can use segmentation and automations to tailor messages to specific audiences, ensuring your outreach feels relevant rather than generic. Mailchimp offers tons of email and form templates designed for different marketing and sales scenarios and business types. Meanwhile, advanced reporting shows you exactly who opened, clicked, or engaged with your emails, so your team knows which leads to follow up with and when. Is Mailchimp a good email marketing platform when managing multiple Shopify stores? Yes. Mailchimp is actually ideal for this situation. We offer over 300 integrations, making it easier to connect your various data sources. You can integrate multiple Shopify stores and other leading e-commerce platforms with one Mailchimp account. With Mailchimp acting as a central hub, you can more easily manage audiences, campaigns, and reports across different shops. The Shopify integration specifically helps unlock the power of your store data by letting you set up automations like welcome series and abandoned cart sequences using information directly from your store. With more e-commerce data flowing into Mailchimp, you get stronger personalization, more automation opportunities, and better overall results. Does Mailchimp's email marketing platform have automation and segmentation? Absolutely. You can set up automated journeys for all kinds of scenarios, including welcome emails when someone subscribes, abandoned cart reminders, and re-engagement campaigns for inactive customers, and more. Advanced segmentation lets you target customers based on their behaviors, purchase history, and preferences, ensuring your messages reach the right people at the right time. This combination of automation and segmentation is what makes modern email marketing strategies so powerful. You're not just blasting the same message to everyone — you're creating personalized experiences that drive better engagement and conversions. Will Mailchimp's email marketing platform integrate well with my CRM? Yes. Mailchimp's email marketing services connect with hundreds of apps, including popular CRMs, so your customer data stays in sync across platforms. That way, you can use the insights from your CRM to personalize campaigns and nurture 