st. Members gain access to essential training, exclusive webinars with Poynter experts and practical tools that support both individual growth and the organizational change needed to thrive in today’s media landscape. Interested in purchasing Poynter Memberships for your staff? Group and corporate options are available. Contact Jamese to start the conversation. What’s in it for You? Nearly $500 in value and a connection to journalism’s premier training institute. Membership includes: Access to Poynter’s Fundamental Online Course Series 8 essential courses on writing, editing and ethics — free only with membership. Whether you’re early in your career or a veteran journalist, these essential asynchronous courses equip you with the skills, tools and knowledge needed to excel in today’s market. Topics include reporting fundamentals, ethics, editing, digital storytelling, audience strategy and more. Members receive free access to: Cleaning Your Copy: Grammar, Style and More The Lead Lab Journalism Fundamentals: Craft & Values The Writer’s Workbench: 50 Tools You Can Use Clear, Strong Writing for Broadcast Journalism Ethics of Journalism Introduction to Reporting: Beat Basics Conducting Interviews That Matter (Approximate value: $200 annually) Members Only Teaching Series (Quarterly) Live, members-only training on critical topics from Poynter experts. The Poynter Pro Teaching Series is a quarterly lineup of live, interactive members-only webinars designed to help you tackle today’s most pressing journalism challenges — from ethics to to AI to leadership and craft. These sessions go beyond lectures, giving members practical guidance and real-world examples they can apply immediately. Each session is led by Poynter faculty and experts, with opportunities to ask questions and engage directly. Members who can’t attend live will receive full access to the recordings. Using AI Effectively — Wednesday, May 27, 2026, 1 p.m. Eastern Navigating Ethical Dilemmas — Wednesday, Sept. 30, 2026, 12 p.m. Eastern Reporting for Detail — Wednesday, Oct. 14, 2026 at 1 p.m. Eastern (Approximate value: $200 annually) The 5 Ws of Research – 2026 Uncover facts others miss and strengthen your reporting with primary-source evidence. The 5 Ws of Research equips you with practical techniques for finding, verifying and using public records and hard-to-access information. Led by the researchers behind PolitiFact, Poynter’s Pulitzer Prize-winning fact-checking organization, this training strengthens your reporting and fact-checking skills from the ground up. This benefit includes a recorded webinar, plus an on-demand research guide you can return to whenever you need it. Whether you’re verifying claims, tracking down public records or strengthening accountability reporting, this training provides tools you can apply immediately. The 5Ws of Research (2026) — Wednesday, July 29, 2026, 1 p.m. Eastern (Approximate value: $75) Early Access to Attend Poynter Events Attend Poynter events, including the Bowtie Ball. Jump the line and secure tickets to Poynter events, including our annual Bowtie Ball in Tampa, Florida. Questions about membership? Visit our FAQ page for answers, or contact Jamese at membership@poynter.org .",
