itle, email and relationship to you. The reference letter itself should be emailed to info@poynter.org no later than one week past the application deadline. More details are within this application. ||| Questions? Email us at info@poynter.org. This field is hidden when viewing the form Date submitted MM slash DD slash YYYY Name * First Last Preferred name (nickname) Job title * Organization * Business email address * Personal email address * Cell phone number * Please include country code if outside the U.S. If no phone number is available, please say none. Work phone number Preferred Address * Home Work Other Street address * City * State * Select Alabama Alaska Arizona Arkansas California Colorado Connecticut Delaware District of Columbia Florida Georgia Hawaii Idaho Illinois Indiana Iowa Kansas Kentucky Louisiana Maine Maryland Massachusetts Michigan Minnesota Mississippi Missouri Montana Nebraska Nevada New Hampshire New Jersey New Mexico New York North Carolina North Dakota Ohio Oklahoma Oregon Pennsylvania Rhode Island South Carolina South Dakota Tennessee Texas Utah Vermont Virginia Washington West Virginia Wisconsin Wyoming Other Postal Code * Country (if other than United States) or U.S. territory Please note that we can accept only English-fluent candidates whose newsrooms have operating structures similar to U.S.-based newsrooms. Section Two: Professional Information Do you have a preference for which program you would like to participate in? * We will attempt to accommodate your preferred program, but it may not be guaranteed. If our selection committee thinks you are a better fit for another program, we will reach out to you directly. Lead with Influence (February 2 - March 9, virtual, weekly) Essential Skills for New Managers (March 1-5, in-person) Poynter Leadership Academy (April 12-16, in-person) Leadership Academy for Women (May 3-7, in-person) Lead with Influence (September 1 - October 6, virtual, weekly) Essential Skills for New Managers (November 8-12, in-person) Poynter can decide which is best for me Brief Bio * Please paste a brief bio (100 words or less) written in third person; be sure to include your current role and organization. (e.g., Dylan Smyth is a City Editor at the Anytown Daily, in Springfield, Illinois. Smyth was previously a Metro Reporter at the Daily and is a graduate of Springfield University.) Briefly explain your leadership role. If you train or otherwise informally manage others (including freelancers, new hires, or interns) or manage projects, please explain how you demonstrate leadership in your organization. * (Limit 100 words.) Have you applied for this program before? * Yes No If yes to the above, please describe how your role/responsibilities have changed since your previous application. * (Limit 100 words.) LinkedIn profile * Are you a manager with direct reports? * Yes No If yes, how many people do you supervise? None 1-5 6-10 More than 10 How many years of people leadership experience do you have over your entire career? * (This can include at other organizations or in other positions.) Less than 1 year 2-3 years 4-5 years 6-10 More than 10 years If more than 10 years, how long? Briefly share why you think you need leadership training at this point in your career. * Please also list any previous leadership training you’ve had. (Limit 200 words.) Tell us what leadership problems you’re trying to solve, what questions you’re hoping to answer through this training, and what skills or competencies you’d like to boost. * (Limit 200 words.) Reference Letter All applicants for our in-person leadership programs must submit a reference letter from their current supervisor or someone who can write about their career trajectory. Please ask them to email this letter to Poynter at info@poynter.org. The subject line should be \"Leadership Program Applicant: Last Name, Reference Letter” * Ask your reference to highlight your current influence as a leader and how this training might impact 