y inform Poynter CFO/COO Jessi Navarro in person, by phone (727-337-7131) or email (jnavarro@poynter.org) if you observe or experience unwelcome and offensive behavior. • Seek permission from anyone involved in a program before quoting them or sharing materials that may have been presented. • Some Poynter events are shared with members of the public; please be respectful to all patrons and staff. Unacceptable Behavior Unacceptable behavior includes, but is not limited to, intimidating, threatening, harassing, abusive, discriminatory, derogatory, demeaning or disorderly conduct; or possession, use or distribution of any illegal substances. Poynter does not tolerate the use or abuse of illegal substances at any of the venues where Poynter events are held. Harassing conduct can take many forms. Sexually harassing conduct can be by a person of the same or opposite sex. Poynter reserves the right in its sole discretion to determine what constitutes unacceptable behavior. Consequences of Unacceptable Behavior Unacceptable behavior will not be tolerated whether by other attendees, media, speakers or venue staff. Anyone asked to stop engaging in unacceptable behavior is expected to comply immediately. If a participant engages in unacceptable behavior, Poynter may take any action it deems appropriate, up to and including immediate expulsion without warning from the event and without refund of any associated fees. What to Do if You Witness or Are Subject to Unacceptable Behavior Harassment will not be tolerated by Poynter. If you are subject to unacceptable behavior, notice that someone else is being subject to unacceptable behavior or have any other concerns, please immediately notify security staff and/or Poynter CFO/COO Jessi Navarro in person, by phone (727-337-7131) or e-mail (jnavarro@poynter.org). Also notify appropriate law enforcement if necessary. Poynter will be available to help participants contact venue security or local law enforcement, to provide escorts, or to otherwise assist those experiencing unacceptable behavior to feel safe for the duration of the event. https://www.poynter.org/poynter-institute-code-ethics/#conduct I certify I have read and understand Poynter's Code of Conduct listed above. Thank you for your application. It will be processed once you press \"submit.\" After the application deadline, we will go through a period of review. No payment is necessary at this time. We will contact you with further details if you are accepted. A copy of this application will be emailed to you as confirmation. Δ Sign In Register Sign into your account Sign In or Register to Enroll - OR - Checkout as a Guest Remember Me Reset Password Don't have an account? Register Sign In Register Register a new account Sign In or Register to Enroll Password should contain at least: Eight characters One uppercase letter One lowercase letter One number One of the following special characters: @ # - _ $ * % ^ & + = § ! ? Already have an account? Sign In Sign In Register Poynter Leadership Academy (2027) $ 1,350.00 Poynter Leadership Academy (2027) quantity Apply Now Leadership St. Petersburg, Fla. Poynter Leadership Academy (2027) Apply by Jan. 18, 2027 , for a five-day, in-person leadership academy for experienced and senior managers ready to strengthen their skills and lead more strategically. Through hands-on training, coaching and peer discussions, you’ll tackle complex leadership challenges, strengthen your organization and expand your impact, April 12–16, 2027, at Poynter’s campus in St. Petersburg, Florida. April 12, 2027 &ndash; April 16, 2027 Overview Submit your application by Jan. 18, 2027. Meet April 12–16, 2027, at Poynter’s campus in St. Petersburg, Florida. Designed for experienced and senior managers ready to strengthen their leadership. Learn directly from Poynter faculty Tony Elkins and Fernanda Camarena. Work through complex leadership challenges through hands-on exercises, strategic conversations and coaching. Build trusted relationships with a cohort of experienced leaders you can turn to long after the program ends. Poynter Leadership Academy (2027) quantity Apply Now SKU: 82700 Tags: At Poynter , Fernanda Camarena , In-person , Leadership , Tony Elkins Learning Outcomes In this program, you will: Develop strategies for talent development, team dynamics and performance management. Learn to share feedback and manage conflict with bosses, peers and direct reports. Practice navigating ethical decision-making in the newsroom. Design leadership and support strategies for intergenerational teams. Prepare to advocate and negotiate for yourself and others. Learn how to delegate with purpose. Assess team burnout and build a toolkit for managing your own. Apply Poynter’s framework for managing work and life. Apply by Jan 18, 2027 $ 1,350.00 Poynter Leadership Academy (2027) quantity Apply Now Overview Submit your application by Jan. 18, 2027. Meet April 12–16, 2027, at Poynter’s campus in St. Petersburg, Florida. Designed for experienced and senior managers ready to strengthen their leadership. Learn directly from Poynter faculty Tony Elkins and Fernanda Camarena. Work through complex leadership challenges through hands-on exercises, strategic conversations and coaching. Build trusted relationships with a cohort of experienced leaders you can turn to long after the program ends. Training 5 or More People? get consulting & coaching Description Schedule Requirements Poynter Leadership Academy is for experienced and senior managers who want to strengthen their leadership skills and think more strategically about their work. If you’re an executive editor, managing editor, product leader, audience strategist or other team leader with direct reports ready to take your skills to the next level, this program is designed for you. Apply if you’re an experienced team leader ready to grow Over five days at Poynter’s campus in St. Petersburg, Florida, you’ll explore advanced strategies for developing talent, strengthening team dynamics, managing performance and navigating conflict. You’ll also practice ethical decision-making, learn how to support intergenerational teams, delegate with purpose, advocate for yourself and others and address burnout. You’ll put what you learn into practice through exercises, strategic conversations and coaching. You’ll also build a trusted community of experienced leaders you can rely on after the program ends.   Why learn leadership with Poynter? The Poynter Institute is a global nonprofit working to strengthen journalism to help address society’s most pressing problems. The world’s top journalists and emerging media leaders rely on the Institute to learn new skills, adopt best practices, better serve audiences, scale operations and foster trustworthy information. Poynter’s leadership training draws on more than 50 years of experience strengthening leaders in media. Our faculty bring deep expertise in management, leadership, individual coaching, self-assessment frameworks, conflict management and more. Every program emphasizes practical, hands-on learning you can put to work immediately, along with intentional cohort building that creates space for meaningful connection and shared experience. Poynter Leadership Academy is part of a broader Poynter leadership track, with programs for different stages and types of leadership in media. Whether you’re leading a project without formal authority, managing people for the first time or taking on greater organizational responsibility, there’s a program designed to help you grow. The leadership track: Lead with Influence : Lead projects and influence others without formal authority; no formal management experience required, happens in February (apply by Jan. 8, 2027) and September (apply by July 9, 2027) Essential Skills for New Managers : Build the fundamentals of managing people; 0-3 years of management experience, happens in March (apply by Dec. 7, 2026) and November (apply by Aug. 16, 2027) Poynter Leadership Academy : Strengthen your skills as an experienced or senior leader; 3+ years of leadership/management experience (apply by Jan. 18, 2027) Leadership Academy for Women : Advanced leadership development centered on the experiences of women; 3+ years of leadership/management experience (apply by Feb. 8, 2027) Questions? If you need assistance, email us at info@poynter.org . The application deadline for the program is Jan. 18, 2027 . Accepted participants will be notified early February , 2027. This in-person-only program takes place April 12-16, 2027, in St. Petersburg, Florida, at the Poynter Institute. Sessions will take place from 9 a.m. to 5 p.m. Eastern time most days. Lunch, refreshments and snacks are provided during the program. Accepted applicants must plan to arrive on site no later than the start date and time and should expect to dedicate uninterrupted time to the program for its duration. Below is a tentative schedule, subject to change: Day 1 | Learning About Your Management Style and Focusing on Strengths Explore your leadership style, identify the strengths you bring to management and connect those insights to how you lead. You’ll examine your Gallup CliftonStrengths results, reflect on your goals for the week and begin building relationships with your cohort. Day 2 | Managing Communication Skills Gain a clearer picture of how others experience your leadership through Poynter’s ViewPoynt 360-degree feedback tool. You’ll review feedback from colleagues, work through your results in a small coaching group and learn practical tools to strengthen your communication and leadership in a changing workplace. Day 3 | Managing the People Strengthen the skills you need to lead people effectively. You’ll practice fair and difficult conversations, work through realistic scenarios with your peers, explore burnout and care, and build stronger approaches to delegation and project management. Day 4 | Ethics and Crisis Develop the judgment and confidence to lead when the stake",
