fter Nvidia contacted investigators FOR SUBSCRIBERS Trump inadvertently led emissions to fall by going to war with Iran, research shows FOR SUBSCRIBERS How Congress’ post-midterms session is shaping up FOR SUBSCRIBERS Big tasks await as Congress returns after Democratic surge FOR SUBSCRIBERS They fled Democratic-run states to escape liberal policies. Then the blue wave hit. FOR SUBSCRIBERS Oregon man charged with taking Utah teen had been accused of sexually abusing 6-year-old FOR SUBSCRIBERS U.S. skips the COP31 climate summit as 1.5C global warming limit slips away Slide 1 of 1 Perez was a technical assistant to the president who had served as a teleprompter operator for Trump since 2016. The CFTC cited what it called Perez’s “exemplary cooperation” in the case when announcing the fine and penalties Friday. Then-White House press secretary Karoline Leavitt in July called the online trades a breach of ethics and “deeply unfortunate and frankly a disgrace.” Perez was placed on leave in July and Leavitt said at the time that “this individual will no longer be here.” Share Add NBC News to Google Phil Helsel Phil Helsel is a reporter for NBC News. Steve Kopack contributed .",
