        "evidenceText": "Dianna Russini gets out the word that she's coming back to work next week - NBC Sports Skip navigation Search Query Submit Search Pro Football Talk Rumor Mill PFT Video PFT PM PFT Live PFT Clips What’s next for Aiyuk after being reinstated? Inside Vikings’ immense offensive struggles Week 9 report cards: GB goes off, Maye struggles Other PFT Content In Broncos-Panthers, replay was used to determine whether replay should be used Mike Florio , Mike Florio , Brandon Aiyuk plans to meet with 49ers at team’s business offices, not team facility Mike Florio , Mike Florio , Christian Watson, Matthew Golden are delivering for the Packers Mike Florio , Mike Florio , Search Query Submit Search Pro Football Talk Rumor Mill PFT Video PFT PM PFT Live PFT Clips What’s next for Aiyuk after being reinstated? Inside Vikings’ immense offensive struggles Week 9 report cards: GB goes off, Maye struggles Other PFT Content In Broncos-Panthers, replay was used to determine whether replay should be used Mike Florio , Mike Florio , Brandon Aiyuk plans to meet with 49ers at team’s business offices, not team facility Mike Florio , Mike Florio , Christian Watson, Matthew Golden are delivering for the Packers Mike Florio , Mike Florio , Profile Login or Create Profile Favorites Menu Favorites Sign up to follow your favorites on all your devices. Sign up Teams AFC East Buffalo Bills Miami Dolphins New England Patriots New York Jets AFC North Baltimore Ravens Cincinnati Bengals Cleveland Browns Pittsburgh Steelers AFC South Houston Texans Indianapolis Colts Jacksonville Jaguars Tennessee Titans AFC West Denver Broncos Kansas City Chiefs Las Vegas Raiders Los Angeles Chargers NFC East Dallas Cowboys New York Giants Philadelphia Eagles Washington Commanders NFC North Chicago Bears Detroit Lions Green Bay Packers Minnesota Vikings NFC South Atlanta Falcons Carolina Panthers New Orleans Saints Tampa Bay Buccaneers NFC West Arizona Cardinals Los Angeles Rams San Francisco 49ers Seattle Seahawks AFC East Buffalo Bills Miami Dolphins New England Patriots New York Jets AFC North Baltimore Ravens Cincinnati Bengals Cleveland Browns Pittsburgh Steelers AFC South Houston Texans Indianapolis Colts Jacksonville Jaguars Tennessee Titans AFC West Denver Broncos Kansas City Chiefs Las Vegas Raiders Los Angeles Chargers NFC East Dallas Cowboys New York Giants Philadelphia Eagles Washington Commanders NFC North Chicago Bears Detroit Lions Green Bay Packers Minnesota Vikings NFC South Atlanta Falcons Carolina Panthers New Orleans Saints Tampa Bay Buccaneers NFC West Arizona Cardinals Los Angeles Rams San Francisco 49ers Seattle Seahawks Rumor Mill Peacock PFT Shop Dianna Russini gets out the word that she’s coming back to work next week By Mike Florio , By Mike Florio     Published November 4, 2026 04:21 PM Facebook Twitter Email The halfway point of the 2026 NFL season arrives this weekend. Next week, Dianna Russini apparently will return to sports media. Per a source with knowledge of the situation, Russini has begun getting the word out to people in the league that she’ll be returning to work “next week.” It’s unclear where she’ll be working, or what she’ll be doing. She resigned from The Athletic in April, one week after photos were published by the New York Post of Russini and Patriots coach Mike Vrabel at a resort in Arizona. In both her comments to the Post and her resignation letter to The Athletic, she denied that there was any type of impropriety. The Athletic conducted a review of her work. Its findings were released in early September. “Russini’s relationship with Vrabel was in clear violation of The Athletic ’s standards,” wrote Mike Semel of The Athletic , who conducted the investigation. “Regardless of whether the relationship was romantic, it was a breach and should have been disclosed.” Beyond the relationship was the manner in which she handled the emergence of the controversy. \"[W]hen first confronted with the photos by The New York Post ,” Semel wrote, “Russini waited two days before telling her editors and managers. She then told a story to explain the photos that did not align with facts, raising issues of trust.” Along the way, a strange story emerged regarding Russini being pulled over for texting while driving — made stranger by her decision to tell the story publicly and embellish the notion that she FaceTimed a head coach for help in getting out of the ticket. So if she’ll be reporting again, she’ll need to restore her own credibility. Especially given the unique set of facts that resulted in her departure from The Athletic . Read Now: Quarterback of the Future \" href=\"https://www.nbcsports.com/nfl/profootballtalk/quarterback-of-the-future\" > Read Now: Quarterback of the Future What happens when two modern-day college football players end up in 1960? They can either find real jobs, or they can try out for the local pro team. WATCH: PFT Live with Mike Florio \" href=\"https://www.nbcsports.com/nfl/profootballtalk/pft-live?utm_tags=nbcs1173\" target=\"_blank\" > WATCH: PFT Live with Mike Florio Watch PFT Live with Mike Florio and Chris Simms for the latest news coming out of the NFL every Monday to Friday at 7 a.m. ET on Peacock and the NBC Sports NOW channel. PFT Top Stories J.J. McCarthy, Cam Skattebo return to full participation Tuesday Charean Williams , Charean Williams , Jaguars waive CB Alijah Huzzie Josh Alper , Josh Alper , Dolphins place QB Malik Willis on IR with core muscle injury Charean Williams , Charean Williams , Vikings announce return of Kirk Cousins Mike Florio , Mike Florio , The Kirk Cousins contract points to a revised deal or termination after 2026 Mike Florio , Mike Florio , Chiefs agree to trade for WR Josh Downs Myles Simmons , Myles Simmons , Close Ad",
