        "contentType": "text/html; charset=UTF-8",
        "pageTitle": "ICANN Fellowship Program 2027 to Attend ICANN89 Policy Forum in Vancouver, Canada (Funded) &#8211; Opportunity Desk",
        "pageDescription": "",
        "evidenceText": "ICANN Fellowship Program 2027 to Attend ICANN89 Policy Forum in Vancouver, Canada (Funded) – Opportunity Desk Close Menu Home Conferences Training Scholarships Undergraduate Short Courses Online Courses Masters/Postgraduate PhD Postdoctoral Study Abroad Study in Africa Study in Asia Study in Australia Study in Europe Study in USA Competitions Awards Grants Fellowships Jobs Internships Volunteering Blog OD Specials OD Live Series Young Person of the Month Mentorship OD Mentors Success Stories How-To General Tips ODIC 2025 ODIC 2025 Application ODIC Judges ODIC 2025 Winners ODIC 2023 Winners ODIC 2022 Winners ODIC 2021 Winners ODIC 2019 Winners ODIC 2018 Winners ODIC 2017 Winners ODIC 2016 Winners Search Asia Africa Australia and Oceania America Europe Deadlines Approaching Facebook X (Twitter) Instagram Tuesday, November 10 Facebook X (Twitter) LinkedIn Instagram Telegram ICANN Fellowship Program 2027 to Attend ICANN89 Policy Forum in Vancouver, Canada (Funded) Jude Ogar November 9, 2026 2 Mins Read Facebook Twitter WhatsApp Pinterest LinkedIn Tumblr Email Telegram Deadline: December 5, 2026 Applications are open for the ICANN Fellowship Program 2027 . The goal of the ICANN Fellowship Program is to strengthen the representation of the multistakeholder model by fostering opportunities for individuals from underserved and underrepresented communities to become active participants in the ICANN community. Fellows are exposed to the workings of the ICANN community, are assigned a mentor, and receive training across different areas of knowledge and skill building before, during, and after an ICANN Public Meeting. Benefits Travel assistance to attend the meeting is also provided. Eligibility Candidates from all regions and sectors are welcome to apply. Be at least 21 years of age by the time of the application submission. Be interested in, or already engaged in, the various components of ‌ICANN‍’s work in policy building, the operation of the Domain Name System and the security and stability of the global Internet Complete mandatory ‌ICANN‍ Learn course(s); NOT be involved in or associated with other ICA‌NN supported travel programs at time of selection Policy Forum applicants must have successfully completed an ICA‍NN Fellowship. Have previously received no more than two fellowships; second and third time fellows must prove their involvement and engagement in one of the ICANN communities. Application The deadline for submission is 5 December 2026 at 23:59 UTC Time. Click here to apply For more information, visit ICANN Fellowship Program . Share. Facebook Twitter WhatsApp LinkedIn Email Pinterest Telegram Previous Article Morgridge Acceleration Program (MAP) Fellowship 2027 (Funded) Next Article QNX Global Hackathon 2026 ($50,000 in prizes) Jude Ogar Website Jude Ogar is an educator and youth development practitioner with years of experience working in the education and youth development space. He is passionate about the development of youth in Africa. Related Posts Wave Winter Research Fellowship 2026-2027 November 10, 2026 Closes in 3 days Career Pathways Initiative Fellowship 2027 November 10, 2026 Closes in 80 days Nature Culture Fellowship 2027 November 10, 2026 Closes in 21 days Search for: Receive Opportunity Alerts! Join over 100,000 email subscribers to receive weekly summary of opportunities. Sign up here . OD YPOM – Sameer Ali Khan Sameer Ali Khan is OD Young Person of the Month – October 2026. Read more . Latest Posts Wave Winter Research Fellowship 2026-2027 Career Pathways Initiative Fellowship 2027 Nature Culture Fellowship 2027 Debt Accountability Journalism Fellowship 2027 for Nigerian Journalists Computation & Cognition Tübingen Summer (CaCTüS) Internship Program 2027 Obama Foundation Leaders Program 2027-2028 Chatham House Research Fellow Africa Programme 2026-2027 QNX Global Hackathon 2026 ($50,000 in prizes) Follow on Twitter Tweets by @OpportunityDesk Follow Us on Social Media Submit Type above and press Enter to search. Press Esc to cancel. Ad Blocker Enabled! Our website is made possible by displaying online advertisements to our visitors. Please support us by disabling your Ad Blocker.",
