        "evidenceText": "The Poynter Report Podcast - Podcast - Apple Podcasts The Poynter Report Podcast Tom Jones 4.9 (50) Politics Biweekly You have questions about the media. We have answers. The Poynter Institute, the worldwide leader in supporting journalism, truth and democracy, opens the curtain for a deep look inside the media world. Join veteran journalist and media critic Tom Jones and his industry insider guests for 20 minutes every other week to feel informed and invested in the most relevant media news. Hosted on Acast. See acast.com/privacy for more information. Latest Episode Newest to Oldest Oldest to Newest Episodes 1d ago 2026 Election Debrief with CNN's John King S7 E4: CNN's National Correspondent John King joins the podcast to talk about what he calls an \"historic epic reckoning\". The man who stands in front of the \"Magic Wall\" discusses what caused the Democratic \"blue tsunami\". King provides insight on races in Ohio, Michigan, North Carolina, Florida and more. Hosted on Acast. See acast.com/privacy for more information. 43m Oct 26 Fact Checking the Midterm Elections S7 E3: Which candidates are telling the truth, and which ones aren't? PolitiFact Editor-in-Chief Katie Sanders joins the podcast with a look at key midterm Senate races. What are the top issues and what are the biggest lies? Hosted on Acast. See acast.com/privacy for more information. 36m Oct 12 Fox News Pentagon Correspondent Jennifer Griffin S7 E2: Longtime Fox News Pentagon Correspondent Jennifer Griffin joins the Poynter Report Podcast to discuss her nearly 30-year career with the network. She also provides frank opinions about restrictive Pentagon press policies and her former Fox colleague, and now Secretary of Defense, Pete Hegseth. Hosted on Acast. See acast.com/privacy for more information. 50m Sep 28 Exclusive Interview with MS NOW's Rachel Maddow S7 E1: Season 7 begins with an exciting interview with MS NOW anchor Rachel Maddow. She joins Tom Jones on the Poynter Report to discuss all things President Trump including his recent White House media ban. Rachel also discusses her new documentary and book. Hosted on Acast. See acast.com/privacy for more information. 39m Jul 20 An Exciting New Source for Health and Wellness Information In the season six finale of The Poynter Report, learn about an exciting new offering from the Poynter Institute. Well Informed is designed for consumers looking for accurate health and wellness information. From the people who bring you PolitiFact, find out how Well Informed will be an advocate for consumers. Hosted on Acast. See acast.com/privacy for more information. 25m Jun 29 What is going on at CBS? Wall Street Journal Media Reporter Isabella Simonetti joins host Tom Jones to discuss the recent turmoil at CBS News. Get insight on the status of 60 Minutes. Also, learn what could be next for CNN. Hosted on Acast. See acast.com/privacy for more information. 24m Jun 8 Covering the 2026 FIFA World Cup This is a must-listen to episode for anyone who enjoys soccer/football. The guest is Laura Williamson, Editor-in-Chief of UK and Europe at The Athletic. Hear about how one of the world’s leading sports news organizations is preparing for one of the biggest sporting events on the planet. Hosted on Acast. See acast.com/privacy for more information. 31m May 18 A Seasoned Journalist Looks Back and Forward S6 E1: Season six kicks off with the former national media writer for the Associated Press, David Bauder. He joins The Poynter Report to reflect on his nearly 40-year career with the wire service. Among the topics: his interviews with members of the Beatles, the winners and losers in the media world, and press coverage of President Trump. Hosted on Acast. See acast.com/privacy for more information. 36m See All (43) Ratings & Reviews 4.9 out of 5 50 Ratings First time listener— I loved it! 12/12/2025 Mikaela N. Just listened to your most recent episode with Sally Jenkins and I found it very intriguing. Love hearing you guys talk about the sports side of journalism and all of the behind-the-scenes of your experiences in your work. Thanks for representing journalism well. Keep up the great work! 😊 12/11/2025 Gabs0701 This podcast is so interesting and insightful! Glad I tuned in The Future of Local News and Americas Growing News Deserts 12/11/2025 emelinmae I really liked this episode of The Poynter Report. It talks about how local news is disappearing in a lot of places and how that affects communities. The hosts explain everything in a way that is easy to follow, even when the topic is serious. As a student studying digital communication, it made me think more about why local news actually matters and how it shapes everyday life. It was interesting, clear, and it kept my attention the whole time. I definitely feel like I learned something from it. Loved this! 12/10/2025 elianajenkins22 I really appreciate how “The Poynter Report Podcast” dives into real issues around science communication and journalism in an accessible way. The hosts are clear and thoughtful, presenting complex ideas with examples that make the topics easy to understand even for someone new to journalism. I especially liked the latest episode (as of this review) because it made me think more deeply about how news is reported and the responsibility of journalists. I’d love to hear more episodes that explore how journalism intersects with ethics, public understanding, and misinformation. Keep up the great work! About You have questions about the media. We have answers. The Poynter Institute, the worldwide leader in supporting journalism, truth and democracy, opens the curtain for a deep look inside the media world. Join veteran journalist and media critic Tom Jones and his industry insider guests for 20 minutes every other week to feel informed and invested in the most relevant media news. Hosted on Acast. See acast.com/privacy for more information. Information Creator Tom Jones Years Active 2024 - 20