        "contentType": "text/html; charset=UTF-8",
        "pageTitle": "African Wildlife Foundation (AWF) Geospatial Leaders Fellowship 2027 &#8211; Opportunity Desk",
        "pageDescription": "",
        "evidenceText": "African Wildlife Foundation (AWF) Geospatial Leaders Fellowship 2027 – Opportunity Desk Close Menu Home Conferences Training Scholarships Undergraduate Short Courses Online Courses Masters/Postgraduate PhD Postdoctoral Study Abroad Study in Africa Study in Asia Study in Australia Study in Europe Study in USA Competitions Awards Grants Fellowships Jobs Internships Volunteering Blog OD Specials OD Live Series Young Person of the Month Mentorship OD Mentors Success Stories How-To General Tips ODIC 2025 ODIC 2025 Application ODIC Judges ODIC 2025 Winners ODIC 2023 Winners ODIC 2022 Winners ODIC 2021 Winners ODIC 2019 Winners ODIC 2018 Winners ODIC 2017 Winners ODIC 2016 Winners Search Asia Africa Australia and Oceania America Europe Deadlines Approaching Facebook X (Twitter) Instagram Wednesday, November 11 Facebook X (Twitter) LinkedIn Instagram Telegram African Wildlife Foundation (AWF) Geospatial Leaders Fellowship 2027 Jude Ogar November 11, 2026 2 Mins Read Facebook Twitter WhatsApp Pinterest LinkedIn Tumblr Email Telegram Deadline: December 14, 2026 Applications are open for the African Wildlife Foundation (AWF) Geospatial Leaders Fellowship 2027 . The AWF Geospatial Leaders Fellowship is a ten-month Pan-African programme that brings together mid-level conservation GIS professionals from NGOs, government agencies, research institutions and community-based organisations who are passionate about using spatial data to protect Africa’s wildlife and wild lands. AWF is an Africa-based global conservation organization protecting wildlife and their habitats as essential parts of a modern and prosperous Africa. They articulate a unique vision of African-led conservation, focusing on solutions that create opportunity for people — not at the expense of wildlife and their habitats, but because of them. Eligibility Be a national of, and currently working in, one of the following eleven countries: Cameroon, Democratic Republic of Congo, Ethiopia, Kenya, Rwanda, Senegal, Sierra Leone, South Africa, Tanzania, Tunisia or Uganda Have at least two years of hands-on GIS experience in conservation, natural resource management or a related field. Be currently employed or attached to an organisation (NGO, government agency, research institution, private sector or community-based organisation) that will host your capstone project, and provide a letter of support from your employer confirming your full participation. Be able to commit to ten months of consistent engagement, including virtual sessions, self-paced learning, mentorship check-ins and a capstone project. Be available to travel to Nairobi, Kenya for the in-person workshop on 13th-20th June 2027. Application Application deadline is Monday, December 14, 2026 at 9:59 PM. Click here to apply For more information, visit AWF Geospatial Leaders Fellowship . Share. Facebook Twitter WhatsApp LinkedIn Email Pinterest Telegram Previous Article Wave Winter Research Fellowship 2026-2027 Next Article Commonwealth Shared Scholarship Programme 2027/2028 to Study in the U.K. (Fully-funded) Jude Ogar Website Jude Ogar is an educator and youth development practitioner with years of experience working in the education and youth development space. He is passionate about the development of youth in Africa. Related Posts ANH Academy Science-Policy Fellowships 2027 (Round 3) November 11, 2026 Closes in 474 days Harvard Kennedy School (HKS) American Service Fellowship 2027 (up to $100,000) November 11, 2026 Closes in 20 days Africa Dyslexia Teacher Fellowship Program 2027 November 11, 2026 Closes in 9 days Search for: Receive Opportunity Alerts! Join over 100,000 email subscribers to receive weekly summary of opportunities. Sign up here . OD YPOM – Sameer Ali Khan Sameer Ali Khan is OD Young Person of the Month – October 2026. Read more . Latest Posts ANH Academy Science-Policy Fellowships 2027 (Round 3) Harvard Kennedy School (HKS) American Service Fellowship 2027 (up to $100,000) Africa Dyslexia Teacher Fellowship Program 2027 Pladis Accelerator Programme 2026 African Development Bank Group Shanghai Ocean University Scholarship Masters Degree Program 2027 Global Youth Mental Health Research Fellowship 2027 Commonwealth Shared Scholarship Programme 2027/2028 to Study in the U.K. (Fully-funded) African Wildlife Foundation (AWF) Geospatial Leaders Fellowship 2027 Follow on Twitter Tweets by @OpportunityDesk Follow Us on Social Media Submit Type above and press Enter to search. Press Esc to cancel. Ad Blocker Enabled! Our website is made possible by displaying online advertisements to our visitors. Please support us by disabling your Ad Blocker.",
