        "pageDescription": "Responses to problems are newsworthy. The Solutions Journalism Network is leading a global shift in journalism focused on advancing rigorous reporting about how people are trying to solve problems and what we can learn from their successes and failures.",
        "evidenceText": "Solutions Journalism Network Skip to main content Who We Are What Is Solutions Journalism? Respectful, Helpful & Fair Ethics Team Board of Directors Funders & Supporters Annual Reports & Financials Careers Impact Explore Our Impact How Solutions Journalism Rebalances the News Programs Climate Democracy Youth Mental Health Addressing Health Disparities Beacons Complicating the Narratives Educators Academies Student Media Challenge University Hubs Learning Lab Introduction to Solutions Journalism Webinar Toolkits & Guides Events & Opportunities Trainers All Resources Directory Solutions Story Tracker What You Can Do Sign Up for Newsletters Learn the Basics of Solutions Journalism Explore Our Programs See Upcoming Events & Opportunities Join the Directory Pitch Your Story Nominate Your Project for an Award Become an Accredited Trainer Teach Solutions Journalism Amplify Solutions in Your Community Events & Opportunities News Blog Solutions Insights Lab My Profile Donate Search Search Search Search Search Search Video file Responses to problems are newsworthy The Solutions Journalism Network is leading a global shift in journalism focused on advancing rigorous reporting about how people are trying to solve problems and what we can learn from their successes and failures. Home What is solutions journalism? Solutions journalism is rigorous and compelling reporting about responses to social problems, which includes these key elements: Response Focuses on a response to a social problem — and on how that response has worked, or why it hasn’t Insight Shows what can be learned from a response and why it matters to a newsroom’s audience Evidence Provides data or qualitative results that indicate effectiveness (or a lack thereof) Limitations Places responses in context; doesn’t shy away from revealing shortcomings Newsletters The Solutions Journalism Network offers newsletters for journalists, educators and everyone interested in how people are responding to problems. Sign up for newsletters Bring solutions journalism to your work Learn Explore how to do solutions journalism and advance your reporting. Teach Bring solutions journalism into your classroom or student newsroom. Amplify Inform conversations in your community with solutions journalism. Founded in 2013 by the award-winning journalists David Bornstein, Tina Rosenberg and Courtney Martin, the Solutions Journalism Network includes: 102,300 Journalists, educators and students trained and using SJN tools 1,585 Fellows 226 Accredited trainers worldwide 5 University hubs 150+ Learning Lab resources Browse events and opportunities Explore more ways to get involved News News post Meet Kavita Chandran, New Southeast Asia Coordinator Announcements News post Constructive News vs. The Doom Loop Network News News post Meet Jamie Bedson, New Deputy Director of the Solutions Insights Lab Announcements Browse more news Upcoming events Event Counterpart's Solutions Lab Training November 12, 2026 Event Climate Peer Network Meeting November 12, 2026 Event ⭐ APPLY NOW: Train-the-Trainers (December 2026 Cohort) November 15, 2026 View more events Discover how people are responding to the world’s problems The Solutions Story Tracker® is the largest collection of solutions journalism: 17,700 stories produced by 10,000 journalists and 2,200 news outlets from 102 countries. The stories cover responses in 199 countries, in 20 languages. This resource is made possible because of a growing movement of journalists who use solutions journalism to illuminate both problems and evidence-based responses to them. Search the Solutions Story Tracker® Story Louisiana's accidental blueprint for restoring its coast Story Aztec methods and crocodiles: How biologists are restoring mangroves in Mexico Story An Innovative Program Connects Maine's Fish Industry to School Food Story How Parents in Boulder, Colorado, Rewrote the Rules on Autism Therapy in School Collection Food Waste Collection Combating Extremism Collection Preventing Mass Shootings Collection Student Mental Health in a Changing World Transforming journalism and communities Journalists in our global network use solutions journalism to strengthen community efficacy, challenge false and harmful stereotypes, build trust and civic engagement, depolarize public discourse and build new sources of revenue. Impact story Solutions journalism broadens public discussion of diabetes management Community engagement & action Impact story County acts on telemedicine challenges identified in reporting Accountability Impact story Rabies solutions story prompts county action and expanded vaccinations Accountability Impact story Affordable housing series sparks new civic partnership Community engagement & action View more impact stories Not finding what you need? We love connecting with new partners and collaborators working toward a more sustainable and equitable world through journalism. Fill out the form to request: Custom training for your team or organization A collaboration on a project or partnership An interview with our team for research or an article Get in Touch",
