        "pageTitle": "Rex Ryan arrested after allegedly hitting pedestrians with truck",
        "pageDescription": "ESPN NFL analyst Rex Ryan faces multiple charges after allegedly running over the feet of pedestrians and then leaving the scene.",
        "evidenceText": "Rex Ryan arrested after allegedly hitting pedestrians with truck Skip to content Credit: Kirby Lee-USA TODAY Sports By Matt Yoder on 11/11/2026 11/11/2026 Less AI and more AA in your search results. ESPN NFL analyst Rex Ryan is facing four charges after being arrested following an incident in Nashville. According to The Tennesseean , Ryan was driving his pickup truck downtown when he allegedly ran over the feet of two pedestrians who were attempting to cross Broadway while the former coach was making a right turn. Of course, anyone in the know will find that to be incredibly ironic given Ryan’s well-documented love of that particular body part. Rex Ryan then drove away from the scene and was chased down by the pedestrians. According to the reports, Ryan then left his vehicle at a stop light to engage in an argument with them before driving away once again. Afterwards, the people who were hit took a photograph of the truck and its license plate and called police. It was later then traced back to Ryan, and he turned himself in to the authorities on Wednesday morning. Naturally, TMZ has already published a photo of his mug shot. The 63-year-old is now facing multiple charges stemming from the incident, including leaving the scene of an accident, failing to give information or render aid, and failing to obey a traffic signal. His bond was set at $6,000. When reached by Awful Announcing for comment about the situation, ESPN issued a statement that said, “We are aware and are in touch with Rex.” Ryan was head coach of the New York Jets and Buffalo Bills during his time in the NFL after winning a Super Bowl as defensive coordinator of the Baltimore Ravens. He has been an ESPN analyst since 2017 as one of the network’s top analysts, appearing on a number of shows including Sunday NFL Countdown and Get Up. Rex Ryan is a self-proclaimed “ toe expert ,” so if anyone should have checked on someone’s feet after being run over by a truck, then it should have been him. About Matt Yoder Matt writes the Awful Announcing 'The A Block' newsletter every Wednesday. Subscribe here . View all posts by Matt Yoder Follow on Twitter Related Content The SEC’s TV ratings dominance is getting scary for the Big Ten Jordon Hudson reportedly sues Airbnb owners over leak of topless Bill Belichick footage The 76ers are either building a superteam or creating a superproblem The Dave Portnoy ‘Big Noon Kickoff’ breakup was always inevitable Recent Posts The league says live match viewers per week increased 93%. The beloved commentator died from an \"acute illness.\" Tomlin stepped away from the Pittsburgh Steelers in January and quickly became a hot media prospect before NBC scooped him up. Credit: Kirby Lee-Imagn Images \"It is so much easier to get an audience and make money [by] appealing to the lowest common denominator of the MAGA-sphere than it is to do it in sports.\" \"Maybe, just maybe, the apology can be as loud as y'all leading y'all shows with this topic.\" Sidebar Popular Posts Five NFL teams play three consecutive primetime games this season; zero did so last year. Mike Florio thinks he knows why Where have you gone, Lee Corso? College football fans falling out of love with Saturday pregame shows Recent Posts The league says live match viewers per week increased 93%. The beloved commentator died from an \"acute illness.\" Tomlin stepped away from the Pittsburgh Steelers in January and quickly became a hot media prospect before NBC scooped him up. Credit: Kirby Lee-Imagn Images \"It is so much easier to get an audience and make money [by] appealing to the lowest common denominator of the MAGA-sphere than it is to do it in sports.\" \"Maybe, just maybe, the apology can be as loud as y'all leading y'all shows with this topic.\"",
