        "evidenceText": "Interpol Crackdown on Migrant Smuggling Nets 262 Arrests | OCCRP Organized Crime • Africa Interpol Crackdown on Migrant Smuggling Nets 262 Arrests November 10, 2026 | 1 min read Share Article &times; Aa Text Settings &times; Text Size Small Medium Large Line Spacing Compact Normal Spacious An Interpol-led operation across 16 countries has resulted in 262 arrests tied to migrant smuggling networks along the Mediterranean Sea and West African Atlantic routes, the agency announced Tuesday. The four-day sweep across North and West Africa, southern Europe, and the Middle East identified 109 potential human trafficking victims, detected 1,715 irregular migrants, and sparked 434 new investigations that are “expected to yield further leads and arrests in the coming weeks and months.” Among the key interventions, Moroccan authorities rescued a vessel carrying 70 stranded migrants—including 30 minors—who had been at sea for six days. In a separate action, Mauritanian law enforcement intercepted a wooden boat carrying 80 passengers and arrested three suspected organizers. November 10, 2026 Share Article: Related Articles 10 years ago Making a Killing Montenegro Opens Weapons Supply Line to Saudi Arabia Sanctions Montenegro 4 years ago Interpol Arrests 75 Suspected Cyber Criminals Organized Crime Italy 4 years ago INTERPOL Seized Smuggled Ivory, Rhino Horns, Pangolin and Tiger Parts Organized Crime United States 10 years ago Making a Killing Montenegro Opens Weapons Supply Line to Saudi Arabia Sanctions Montenegro 4 years ago Interpol Arrests 75 Suspected Cyber Criminals Organized Crime Italy 4 years ago INTERPOL Seized Smuggled Ivory, Rhino Horns, Pangolin and Tiger Parts Organized Crime United States Help us improve the website! Click below to give us input. It’ll only take 5 minutes. 👉 Help OCCRP Don't show this anymore",
