        "pageTitle": "High-Profile Smuggling Raids in Hungary Point to Former PM&#039;s Brother | OCCRP",
        "pageDescription": "Police arrested multiple suspects Monday in an alleged visa fraud operation, with local media and politicians quickly linking the sweep to &Aacute;ron Orb&aacute;n.",
        "evidenceText": "High-Profile Smuggling Raids in Hungary Point to Former PM's Brother | OCCRP Organized Crime • Hungary High-Profile Smuggling Raids in Hungary Point to Former PM's Brother Police arrested multiple suspects Monday in an alleged visa fraud operation, with local media and politicians quickly linking the sweep to Áron Orbán. Banner: MZaplotnik / Wikimedia Commons | Hungarian police in Budapest. Reported by Zdravko Ljubas OCCRP November 9, 2026 | 1 min read Share Article &times; Aa Text Settings &times; Text Size Small Medium Large Line Spacing Compact Normal Spacious Hungarian authorities arrested multiple suspects in coordinated human smuggling raids on Monday morning, an operation that local media and political figures say resulted in the detention of Áron Orbán, the younger brother of former Prime Minister Viktor Orbán. The National Bureau of Investigation (NNI) and the National Asset Recovery and Asset Protection Office (NVVH) conducted simultaneous house searches across Budapest and Pest County. While police confirmed the multi-agency operation in a public statement , they did not immediately release the identities of those detained. News outlet Kontroll.hu reported that the former premier's brother may have been among those arrested in connection with an NVVH probe into a visa facilitation network. The reports prompted a public exchange between the former premier and current Prime Minister Péter Magyar. Viktor Orbán indirectly confirmed his brother's arrest in a Facebook post , condemning the police action as a politically motivated \"settling of scores\" designed to distract from an \"agent scandal\" facing the current government. \"In this dirty game, the goal is the elimination of the political opponent and the establishment of a one-party system,\" the former prime minister stated, likening the authorities to Hungary's historical state secret police. \"I am the target, my younger brother is just a tool.\" Current Prime Minister Péter Magyar responded in a Facebook post, criticizing the former leader for deflecting blame and playing the victim. \"As you sow, so shall you reap,\" Magyar wrote. November 9, 2026 Share Article: Reported by Zdravko Ljubas OCCRP Related Articles 4 weeks ago UK Freezes £30 Million Mansion Linked to Alleged Senior Prince Group Associate Organized Crime United Kingdom 3 days ago Interpol Crackdown on Migrant Smuggling Nets 262 Arrests Organized Crime Africa 3 weeks ago Smugglers Collected Up to $509M on Europe Routes in 2025 Organized Crime Europe 4 weeks ago UK Freezes £30 Million Mansion Linked to Alleged Senior Prince Group Associate Organized Crime United Kingdom 3 days ago Interpol Crackdown on Migrant Smuggling Nets 262 Arrests Organized Crime Africa 3 weeks ago Smugglers Collected Up to $509M on Europe Routes in 2025 Organized Crime Europe Help us improve the website! Click below to give us input. It’ll only take 5 minutes. 👉 Help OCCRP Don't show this anymore",
