        "evidenceText": "Bill Simmons Canceled ChatGPT Partnership After Fan Backlash - Bloomberg OpenAI: Trade Secret Fight ChatGPT Wallet Data Center Strategy Shifts ‘Black Box’ Revenue Patient IPO Planning New Model Debut Halted Back Forward Technology Bill Simmons, founder and chief executive officer of the Ringer, experimented with AI on a couple of shows but eventually decided it wasn’t a good fit with his audience. Photographer: Kyle Grillot/Bloomberg Gift this article Contact us: Provide news feedback or report an error Confidential tip? Send a tip to our reporters Site feedback: Take our Survey By Ashley Carman November 12, 2026 at 8:40 PM UTC Save Takeaways by Bloomberg AI In August, Sean Fennessey and Amanda Dobbins, hosts of the Ringer’s show The Big Picture , sat down with podcaster Sam Fragoso to chat about upcoming movie releases. About an hour in, Fragoso raised a question that had been on the minds of many Ringer fans — how did Fennessey and Dobbins feel about their boss, Bill Simmons, promoting OpenAI’s ChatGPT on-air? Simmons, the Ringer’s chief executive officer, had used the artificial intelligence product to mimic storied film critic Roger Ebert, who died in 2013, and guess what he’d have to say about a film. Fennessey, co-host of The Rewatchables with Simmons, said he was uncomfortable with the tactic. Home BTV+ Market Data Opinion Audio Originals Magazine Events News Markets Economics Technology Politics Green Crypto AI Work & Life Wealth Pursuits Businessweek CityLab Sports Equality Management & Work Market Data Stocks Commodities Rates & Bonds Currencies Futures Sectors Economic Calendar Explore Newsletters Explainers Pointed News Quiz Alphadots Game The Big Take Graphics Submit a Tip About Us Terms of Service Do Not Sell or Share My Personal Information Trademarks Privacy Policy Careers Advertise Ad Choices Help ©2026 Bloomberg L.P. All Rights Reserved.",
